// "Key takeaways" shown at the top of each article (keyed by post slug). 3 short, factual bullets.
module.exports = {
  'what-is-generative-engine-optimisation': ['GEO is the work of making your business easy for AI assistants to understand, trust and cite in their answers.', 'It builds on SEO foundations: clear pages, consistent facts, structured data and authority from trusted websites.', 'Start with your most important pages: answer questions directly, state facts plainly and make sure they match everywhere online.'],
  'website-redesign-without-losing-rankings': ['Most ranking losses after a redesign come from changed URLs without redirects, removed content and technical mistakes at launch.', 'Benchmark before you start, map every important old URL to its new home with a 301 redirect, and keep the content that ranks.', 'Test on staging, launch at a quiet time and monitor Search Console closely for the first weeks after launch.'],
  'shopify-vs-woocommerce-uk': ['Shopify suits sellers who want a hosted, low-maintenance store; WooCommerce suits those who want full control and already use WordPress.', 'Compare total cost over two to three years, including apps, plugins, hosting, payment fees and maintenance, not just the monthly plan.', 'Both can rank well and handle UK VAT, payments and shipping; the right choice depends on your catalogue, team and growth plans.'],
  'linkedin-ads-b2b-lead-generation-uk': ['LinkedIn&rsquo;s strength is professional targeting by job title, seniority, industry and company, which suits B2B offers with a clear audience.', 'Clicks cost more than on many platforms, so the offer, creative and follow-up process decide whether it pays off.', 'Measure cost per qualified lead and pipeline, not cost per click, and connect LinkedIn leads to your CRM.'],
  'how-to-choose-a-digital-marketing-agency-uk': ['Start with your goals and budget, then look for an agency whose services, sectors and way of working fit them, not the other way round.', 'Ask for specifics: what is delivered each month, who does the work, how results are reported and who owns your accounts.', 'Treat guarantees, vague proposals and long lock-ins without review points as warning signs.'],
  'how-much-does-seo-cost-uk': ['Most UK SEO is sold as a monthly retainer; the price reflects hours, content volume and how competitive your market is.', 'A cheap quote is only good value if the scope is clear: ask exactly what is delivered each month and how progress is reported.', 'SEO typically takes 3&ndash;6 months to show meaningful results, so budget for at least that long before judging it.'],
  'hotel-direct-bookings-uk': ['Direct bookings start with a fast, mobile-friendly website where the booking button is always visible and the booking engine is simple.', 'Google is where many guests decide: a complete Business Profile, accurate details and brand-name ads protect your direct channel.', 'Give guests a reason to book direct, such as flexible terms, perks or best-rate assurance, and keep past guests close with email.'],
  'google-shopping-ads-guide-uk': ['Shopping ads run on your product feed rather than ad copy and chosen keywords, so product data shapes when your items appear.', 'You need Merchant Center, a linked Google Ads account, accurate product data and conversion tracking before you start.', 'Begin with a focused campaign on profitable products, and judge it on margin rather than revenue alone.'],
  'fca-compliant-marketing-financial-advisers': ['Marketing from regulated firms is generally treated as a financial promotion: it must be fair, clear and not misleading, and approved through your compliance process.', 'Educational content, clear fee information and well-structured adviser websites support both compliance and lead generation.', 'Build compliance sign-off into the workflow from the start, so campaigns are not delayed or rewritten at the last minute.'],
  'ecommerce-website-cost-uk': ['An ecommerce website has two kinds of cost: the one-off build and the ongoing running costs. Budget for both.', 'Product volume, custom features, integrations and design complexity are what move a quote up or down.', 'A clear brief with your product count, must-have features and integrations is the fastest way to an accurate price.'],
  'digital-pr-link-building-uk': ['Digital PR earns links by giving journalists something genuinely worth covering: data, expertise, a timely angle or a useful resource.', 'Relevance beats volume: a few links from respected sites in your sector or region are worth more than many from unrelated blogs.', 'Measure coverage, links, referral traffic and branded search, and judge campaigns over months rather than days.'],
  'ecommerce-seo-agency-uk': ['A good ecommerce SEO agency focuses on category pages, product pages and technical health, because that is where most organic revenue comes from.', 'Expect a monthly retainer, with meaningful movement in rankings and organic sales typically showing within 3 to 6 months.', 'Choose an agency that reports on revenue and orders from organic search, not just rankings, and that can explain its plan for your catalogue in plain English.'],
  'google-ads-agency-uk': ['A good Google Ads agency starts with your margins, tracking and landing pages, not with keywords and bids.', 'In-house suits large, steady accounts; an agency suits businesses that need specialist skills without a permanent hire.', 'Ask who works on your account, who owns it, how results are measured and how you can leave.'],
  'healthcare-marketing-agency-uk': ['Healthcare marketing in the UK must respect ASA and CAP Code rules, platform policies and professional guidance, with final sign-off resting with the clinic.', 'Local SEO, a strong Google Business Profile and clear treatment pages usually do the heavy lifting for private clinics.', 'Choose an agency that expects your team to approve claims, keeps accounts in your name and never promises patient outcomes or rankings.'],
  'local-seo-uk-guide': ['Your Google Business Profile is the foundation of local SEO: verify it, choose accurate categories and keep it complete and active.', 'Consistent name, address and phone details plus a steady flow of genuine reviews build the trust Google looks for in local results.', 'Location pages work only when each one is genuinely useful to people in that area; thin pages with swapped town names do more harm than good.'],
  'ppc-management-cost-uk': ['PPC management in the UK is usually charged as a percentage of ad spend, a flat monthly fee or a retainer, and your ad spend is always paid on top.', 'The fee only makes sense once you know what is included: tracking, search term reviews, testing, landing page advice and reporting.', 'Walk away from agencies that hold your ad account, lock you into long contracts or promise fixed results.'],
  'saas-seo-agency-uk': ['SaaS SEO works best when content is product-led: it solves real problems and shows how your product helps.', 'Comparison, alternative and integration pages target buyers close to choosing a tool, so they often matter more than top-of-funnel traffic.', 'Measure SEO by sign-ups, trials and demos influenced, not just traffic, and allow 3 to 6 months for results to build.'],
  'seo-for-small-business-uk': ['Start with the basics: a fast, mobile-friendly site, a complete Google Business Profile and one clear page for each service you sell.', 'A small business can do a lot of SEO itself, but an agency saves time on technical work, content planning and link building.', 'Budget for months, not weeks: SEO results typically show within 3 to 6 months, so plan cash flow and expectations accordingly.'],
  'shopify-seo-uk': ['Collections are usually your most valuable Shopify pages for SEO, so give each one a clear title, helpful copy and strong internal links.', 'Shopify creates duplicate product URLs through collection paths; make sure your theme links to the canonical /products/ URL.', 'Every app adds code, so audit apps regularly and remove anything that slows the store without earning its keep.'],
  'technical-seo-audit-checklist': ['Audit in order: crawling, then indexing, then speed and page experience, then redirects and structured data; fixes higher up unlock everything below.', 'Google Search Console is the most important free tool for a technical audit, because it shows what Google actually sees.', 'Prioritise fixes by impact on revenue-driving pages rather than trying to clear every warning a crawler reports.'],
  'website-design-cost-small-business-uk': ['Our small business websites cost £1,000 to £2,000 and online shops £1,500 to £3,500, typically delivered in 3 to 5 weeks and 5 to 12 weeks respectively.', 'Page count, custom design, content, integrations and SEO set-up drive most of the price difference between quotes.', 'Budget for hosting, domains, software, maintenance and content updates, not just the build.'],
  'b2b-marketing-agency-uk': ['A good B2B marketing agency measures success in qualified leads and pipeline, not clicks or impressions, and agrees what counts as a qualified lead before spending anything.', 'Most UK B2B firms do best with a small mix of channels: search for buyers already looking, LinkedIn for reaching named job titles, and content that helps a buying committee decide.', 'Long sales cycles mean results compound slowly, so expect organic work to take 3 to 6 months and judge paid channels on lead quality over several months.'],
  'brand-strategy-agency-uk': ['A brand strategy agency helps you decide who you serve, what you stand for and how you sound, so every page, ad and post pulls in the same direction.', 'Useful deliverables are practical: positioning, messaging, tone of voice and a simple guide your team will actually use.', 'Strategy should feed straight into your website, content and campaigns, otherwise it becomes a document nobody opens.'],
  'content-marketing-agency-uk': ['A content marketing agency plans, writes and promotes content that answers real customer questions, so you are found in search and trusted when people compare options.', 'Pricing usually comes as a monthly retainer, a per-piece rate or a project fee; compare what each includes rather than the headline number.', 'Measure content ROI against enquiries and sales, not just traffic, and give it 3 to 6 months before judging results.'],
  'ecommerce-marketing-agency-uk': ['An ecommerce marketing agency joins up channels such as SEO, Google Shopping, paid social, email and conversion work around profitable sales.', 'A specialist ad or paid search agency may be enough if organic and on-site work are already covered in-house.', 'Judge any agency on revenue, margin and returning customers rather than traffic, and keep ownership of your accounts and data.'],
  'education-marketing-agency-uk': ['Education marketing is built around recruitment calendars, so search, paid ads and content need to peak before open days, application deadlines and course start dates.', 'Parents, learners and employers search differently, so course pages, fees information and next steps should be written for each audience.', 'Measure success in enquiries, open day bookings and applications rather than traffic, and allow typically 3 to 6 months for SEO to build.'],
  'financial-adviser-seo-uk': ['SEO for financial advisers works best when it targets local and specialist searches, such as pension or retirement advice in a named town, rather than broad national terms.', 'Trust signals matter more in financial services: clear adviser information, regulatory status, fees explained in plain English and genuinely helpful content.', 'Every page and article should go through the firm\'s own compliance sign-off, and results typically take 3 to 6 months to build.'],
  'hospitality-marketing-agency-uk': ['Hospitality marketing lives or dies on local search, reviews and a fast mobile booking journey, because most guests decide on their phone.', 'Hotels, restaurants and event venues need different plans: direct bookings for hotels, covers and reservations for restaurants, enquiries for venues.', 'Measure bookings, covers and enquiries by channel, and plan campaigns ahead of seasonal peaks rather than reacting when they arrive.'],
  'shopify-agency-uk': ['A good Shopify agency starts with your products, margins and customers, not with a theme, and should explain exactly what is in scope before work begins.', 'Compare agencies on process, ownership of the store, SEO migration care and aftercare, not just on the headline build price.', 'A focused Shopify build for a UK small business typically takes 5 to 12 weeks, and our published ecommerce site price is £1,500 to £3,500.'],
  'website-maintenance-uk': ['Website maintenance is routine care that keeps a site secure, fast, backed up and accurate; support is the help you get when something breaks or needs changing.', 'A monthly checklist of updates, backups, form tests, search checks and renewals covers the essentials, whoever does the work.', 'Compare providers on included tasks, response times and who owns the domain, hosting and licences, not just the monthly figure.'],
  'woocommerce-agency-uk': ['WooCommerce suits UK businesses that want full control of their site, already run WordPress or need content and shop working closely together.', 'Because you host and maintain WooCommerce yourself, a good agency plans hosting, security, backups and updates as part of the build, not as an afterthought.', 'Our published ecommerce site price is £1,500 to £3,500, with builds typically taking 5 to 12 weeks depending on range and integrations.'],
  'digital-pr-agency-uk': ['Digital PR earns coverage and links by giving journalists genuinely newsworthy stories, data and expert comment, not by buying placements.', 'Judge an agency on the relevance and quality of coverage, referring domains and brand mentions, not on raw link counts or vanity reach figures.', 'Ask for the full process up front: ideation, data, outreach lists, reporting and what happens when a campaign does not land.'],
  'geo-agency-uk': ['A GEO agency works to get your brand cited and recommended in AI answers, building on solid SEO rather than replacing it.', 'Core GEO work covers answer-ready content, structured data, entity consistency, third-party mentions and tracking AI citations.', 'Be wary of agencies promising guaranteed AI rankings; ask how they measure citations and how GEO connects to your existing SEO.'],
  'link-building-cost-uk': ['Link building cost depends far more on the method used than on the number of links promised, so compare tactics before comparing prices.', 'Earned links from digital PR, content and relationships carry far less risk than bought links, private blog networks or unqualified sponsored posts.', 'Cheap per-link packages and guaranteed volumes are the clearest red flags; ask for every live URL and the reasoning behind each target page.'],
  'seo-agency-vs-freelancer-uk': ['Freelancers suit focused, well-defined SEO needs; agencies suit broader scopes needing several skills; in-house suits sustained, large-scale programmes.', 'Compare total cost and continuity risk, not just the monthly fee: holidays, illness, staff turnover and management time all have a price.', 'Whichever route you choose, insist on clear scope, access to your own accounts and reporting tied to enquiries and revenue.'],
  'seo-audit-cost-uk': ['SEO audit cost depends on site size, platform complexity and depth: an automated scan is not the same as a prioritised, expert-reviewed audit.', 'A useful audit covers technical health, content, authority, local or ecommerce specifics and AI search readiness, with every issue ranked by impact.', 'The audit is only valuable if it is implemented, so budget for fixes and ask who will make the changes before you commission one.'],
  'ecommerce-cro-uk': ['Start with the checkout and product pages, where small fixes affect every order and every paid click.', 'Use research before testing: analytics, recordings, surveys and support questions show where shoppers get stuck.', 'Only A/B test when traffic allows; smaller UK stores should make evidence-based fixes and measure before and after.'],
  'google-shopping-agency-uk': ['Most Shopping performance is decided by the product feed, so ask any agency how they manage titles, attributes and errors.', 'Merchant Center health (approvals, policies, shipping and returns) is ongoing work, not a one-off setup task.', 'Judge agencies on feed process, campaign structure and reporting by product margin, not on promises of ROAS.'],
  'meta-ads-agency-uk': ['Meta ads work best when you have a visual product, a clear offer and enough budget to test several creatives at once.', 'Tracking comes first: the Meta pixel, the Conversions API and clean events decide how well the algorithm can optimise.', 'Compare agencies on creative testing process, reporting and what the fee covers, and remember ad spend is always paid separately.'],
  'performance-max-guide-uk': ['Performance Max is only as good as its inputs: conversion values, product feed, audience signals and creative assets.', 'Asset groups should be built around product themes or margin bands, not one group for the whole catalogue.', 'Protect against the common pitfalls: brand traffic inflating results, weak feeds, too little data and no exclusions.'],
  'ppc-audit-checklist': ['Audit conversion tracking first: every other finding depends on whether the numbers are right.', 'Work from symptoms to causes: a symptom-to-fix table stops you changing bids when the real problem is the landing page.', 'Run a light audit monthly and a full audit quarterly or before any change of agency or budget.'],
  'dental-marketing-uk': ['Local search and a well-run Google Business Profile are the foundation of dental marketing, because most patients choose a practice nearby.', 'Each private treatment deserves its own clear, factual page with fees, process and what to expect.', 'Dental advertising is regulated, so final approval of claims should rest with the practice and its compliance advisers.'],
  'digital-marketing-agency-cost-uk': ['Most UK agencies charge a monthly retainer for ongoing work and a fixed project fee for builds such as websites.', 'Price is driven by scope, channels, competition and how much senior time you get, not by the agency\'s logo.', 'Compare quotes line by line: deliverables, reporting, who owns the accounts and whether ad spend sits outside the fee.'],
  'marketing-agency-contract-uk': ['Read the term, notice period and renewal clauses first, because they decide how easily you can leave.', 'Make sure ad accounts, analytics, domains, websites and content are owned by your business, not the agency.', 'This is general information only: have a qualified solicitor review any contract before you sign it.'],
  'marketing-agency-for-startups-uk': ['Get positioning, a clear website and working analytics in place before spending heavily on ads or SEO.', 'Match channels to your stage: validate demand first, then build compounding channels such as search and content.', 'Keep every account in the company\'s name and agree a small, measurable scope you can scale up later.'],
  'restaurant-marketing-uk': ['Google Business Profile is often the first thing diners see, so keep hours, menu, photos and booking link accurate.', 'Make booking direct and easy, and publish the menu as readable text, not just a PDF or photo.', 'Reviews, local SEO and a steady social presence keep the restaurant visible between busy periods.'],
  'ga4-setup-uk': ['A useful GA4 setup tracks a short list of key events that reflect real business outcomes, such as enquiries, calls and purchases.', 'UK sites generally need a consent banner for analytics and advertising cookies under PECR, and Google consent mode helps tags respect those choices.', 'Link GA4 to Google Ads and Search Console, test every event, and review data monthly.'],
  'landing-page-design-uk': ['A strong landing page matches the ad that sent the click, makes one clear offer and asks for one action.', 'Structure matters more than decoration: headline, proof, benefits, objections and a short form or button.', 'Test one meaningful change at a time and judge results on leads or sales, not clicks.'],
  'website-redesign-cost-uk': ['A small business website redesign typically costs around £1,000 to £2,000, and an ecommerce redesign around £1,500 to £3,500.', 'Page count, content, integrations, platform changes and migration work drive most of the cost.', 'Budget for SEO migration from day one: redirects and checks cost far less than lost rankings.'],
  'website-speed-optimisation-uk': ['Website speed optimisation starts with measuring Core Web Vitals on real mobile users: LCP, INP and CLS.', 'Most slow UK small business sites suffer from oversized images, too many scripts and plugins, and weak hosting.', 'Fix the biggest bottleneck first, retest, and keep speed in your maintenance routine so it does not slip back.'],
  'wordpress-agency-uk': ['A strong WordPress agency in the UK keeps plugins to a minimum, builds on a maintained theme and hands you full ownership of the site and hosting.', 'Small WordPress websites typically sit around £1,000 to £2,000 and WooCommerce stores around £1,500 to £3,500, with builds taking 3 to 5 or 5 to 12 weeks.', 'Ask about security, updates, backups, speed and SEO migration before you sign, not after launch.'],
  'ai-marketing-agency-uk': ['AI speeds up research, analysis, drafting and testing; strategy, judgement, brand voice and accountability stay with people.', 'Ask any AI marketing agency exactly which tasks use AI, how outputs are checked and how your data is protected.', 'Judge an AI-powered agency on the same outcomes as any agency: clear goals, honest reporting and results over time.'],
  'amazon-seo-agency-uk': ['Marketplace search rewards relevance and sales performance, so keyword-rich listings only work when images and price convert.', 'Titles, bullet points, backend search terms, item specifics and A+ content each play a different role; treat them as one system.', 'Keep marketplace and website SEO joined up: the same keyword research and product data should feed both.'],
  'shopify-plus-migration-uk': ['A full URL inventory and one-to-one 301 redirect map is the single biggest protection for rankings during a migration.', 'Migrate customers, orders, products, reviews and content in tested passes, with a staging review before launch.', 'Monitor Search Console, crawl errors and revenue daily for the first weeks and fix issues fast.'],
  'tiktok-ads-agency-uk': ['TikTok works best for visual, impulse-friendly products with a clear hook and a margin that can absorb testing.', 'Creative is the targeting on TikTok: plan for a steady supply of native, vertical videos rather than one polished advert.', 'Set up the TikTok Pixel, Events API and GA4 before spending, and judge results on blended revenue, not platform numbers alone.'],
  'youtube-ads-agency-uk': ['Pick the YouTube format by goal: skippable in-stream and Shorts for action, bumpers for reach, in-feed for consideration.', 'The first five seconds decide most YouTube results, so brief the opening before anything else.', 'Measure YouTube with conversions, view-through signals, branded search and blended revenue, not views alone.'],
  'b2b-seo-uk': ['Start with bottom-of-funnel pages such as services, use cases, comparisons and pricing, because those are the searches closest to a sales conversation.', 'B2B keywords often have tiny search volumes, so judge them by deal value and intent rather than traffic.', 'Measure B2B SEO by enquiries and pipeline, which means joining up analytics with your CRM.'],
  'charity-marketing-uk': ['Google Ad Grants can give eligible charities free search advertising, but the account needs careful structure and tracking to stay compliant and useful.', 'Fundraising and volunteer pages should be fast, focused and easy to complete on a phone, because supporters often look for charities there.', 'UK GDPR, PECR and the Code of Fundraising Practice shape how charities collect data and ask for support, so check guidance before you launch campaigns.'],
  'ecommerce-email-marketing-uk': ['Automated flows such as welcome, abandoned basket and post-purchase usually matter more than one-off campaigns, so build them first.', 'Segment by what customers do (purchases, browsing, engagement) rather than sending every email to the whole list.', 'UK consent rules under PECR and UK GDPR shape who you can email and how, so check your sign-up wording and get advice if unsure.'],
  'google-business-profile-uk': ['Your primary category is the single biggest setting on your profile, so choose the most specific one that describes what you actually do.', 'Reviews, photos and posts work best as a steady weekly habit rather than a one-off burst before a busy season.', 'A profile only performs if it agrees with your website and directory listings on name, address, phone number and opening hours.'],
  'saas-ppc-uk': ['Optimise SaaS PPC to qualified trials, demos and paying customers, not just form fills, by feeding CRM data back into the ad platforms.', 'Google Search captures existing demand while LinkedIn reaches buyers by role and company, so most B2B SaaS teams need both in different proportions.', 'Competitor and alternative terms can be valuable, but use fair, accurate ad copy and avoid using trade marks in ways that breach platform policy.'],
  'mortgage-broker-marketing-uk': ['Own your leads through local SEO, helpful content and referrals rather than relying only on bought-in lead lists.', 'Paid search works best on specific, high-intent terms such as first-time buyer, remortgage and buy-to-let in your area.', 'Websites, ads and social posts are financial promotions, so the firm or its network must approve them before publishing.'],
  'private-clinic-marketing-uk': ['Local search and a complete Google Business Profile drive most new patient enquiries for physio, aesthetics and private GP clinics.', 'Clear treatment pages with fees, practitioner details and what to expect build the trust patients need before booking.', 'Health advertising is regulated, so final approval of claims should rest with the clinic and its compliance advisers.'],
  'rebranding-guide-uk': ['Start with the reason for the rebrand and a clear brand strategy, not a new logo.', 'Tell existing customers early and explain what changes for them and what stays the same.', 'Protect search rankings with a full redirect map, updated listings and checks for weeks after launch.'],
  'school-marketing-uk': ['Treat marketing as an admissions funnel, from first search to open day to registration, and measure each stage.', 'Open days are the main conversion point, so plan campaigns, booking forms and follow-up around them.', 'Local SEO, honest fees information and a fast mobile website do more for enquiries than glossy brochures alone.'],
  'training-provider-marketing-uk': ['Each course needs its own detailed page that answers price, format, dates, entry requirements and outcomes.', 'Paid search on specific, high-intent course terms usually beats broad awareness campaigns for enrolments.', 'Speed of follow-up and a simple booking or enquiry flow often decide whether an enquiry becomes an enrolment.'],
  'conversion-rate-optimisation-agency-uk': ['A good CRO agency starts with research into where and why visitors drop out, not with a list of button colours to test.', 'A/B testing needs enough traffic; smaller UK sites often get more from evidence-led fixes measured before and after.', 'Judge agencies on their research process, how they handle tracking and consent, and how they report on revenue or leads.'],
  'ecommerce-ppc-agency-uk': ['Ecommerce PPC is built around your product feed, margins and profit, not just clicks and return on ad spend.', 'A good agency covers Google Shopping, Performance Max, search, and social where it fits, with tracking you can trust.', 'Ask how they measure profit, who owns the accounts and what you get each month before signing.'],
  'hotel-seo-uk': ['Hotel SEO starts with your Google Business Profile, accurate details everywhere and a fast, mobile-friendly booking path.', 'Build pages around how guests actually search: location, occasion, room type and nearby attractions or venues.', 'Treat organic search as the channel that lowers your reliance on commission-based booking sites over time.'],
  'local-seo-agency-uk': ['Local SEO agencies focus on your Google Business Profile, location pages, citations, reviews and local links.', 'Multi-location and service-area businesses need a clear plan for location pages that avoids thin, duplicated content.', 'Choose an agency that reports on calls, enquiries and bookings, not just map rankings, and that leaves you owning your profiles.'],
  'seo-migration-checklist': ['Benchmark and crawl the old site first, so you know every URL, ranking and conversion you need to protect.', 'A one-to-one redirect map from every old URL to its closest new equivalent is the single most important task.', 'Monitor closely for at least eight weeks after launch and fix redirect errors, missing pages and tracking gaps quickly.'],
  'accountant-marketing-uk': ['Choose the client types you want most and build service pages and content around their specific needs.', 'Local SEO and Google Business Profile matter for most practices, because many clients still want someone nearby.', 'Deadline-driven content and email around Self Assessment and year end keep you visible when demand peaks.'],
  'estate-agent-marketing-uk': ['Portals bring buyers and tenants; your own marketing should focus on winning vendors and landlords.', 'Valuation landing pages, local SEO and area guides give owners a reason to contact you directly.', 'Property advertising must be accurate and include required information, so check listings and ads before they go live.'],
  'law-firm-marketing-uk': ['Build a separate, genuinely useful page for each practice area and location you want enquiries for.', 'Paid search works for urgent legal needs, but only with tight keywords, negatives and fast enquiry handling.', 'Professional conduct rules apply to how firms promote themselves, so the firm should review and approve every claim.'],
  'professional-services-seo-uk': ['Map each service and sector you want to grow to its own page, built around how clients actually search.', 'Expertise and trust signals, such as named qualifications and accurate team information, matter more than volume of content.', 'In regulated professions, the firm should approve every claim, and SEO copy should never overstate outcomes.'],
  'property-developer-marketing-uk': ['Start building a register of interest well before launch, using a dedicated development site and targeted ads.', 'Paid social and search campaigns should follow the sales stages: awareness, registration, launch and final plots.', 'CGIs, specifications and claims must be accurate and approved by the developer, as property advertising rules apply.'],
  'digital-marketing-agency-leeds': ['Decide which channels you actually need, such as SEO, paid search, social ads or a new website, before you compare Leeds agencies, so you are comparing like with like.', 'A good digital marketing agency builds one joined-up plan across channels and reports on leads and sales, not separate channel reports that never connect.', 'Remote working suits most digital marketing, as long as there is a single point of contact, a regular call and shared reporting.'],
  'ecommerce-agency-bristol': ['Many Bristol online brands are independent, values-led and selling nationally, so the agency needs to build a store that tells your story and sells across the UK, not just locally.', 'Check platform experience, product data handling, checkout and delivery setup, and what support looks like after launch before you sign.', 'Ecommerce builds and growth work are done online, so a remote UK agency can deliver them well with clear milestones, a staging site and regular calls.'],
  'seo-agency-birmingham': ['Many Birmingham and West Midlands firms sell to other businesses, so SEO should focus on specific services, specifications and buyer questions rather than broad city keywords.', 'Compare agencies by asking each for the same three things: what they would fix first, which searches they would target, and how they would report on enquiries.', 'A remote UK agency can handle Birmingham SEO well if you share your market knowledge and agree a clear monthly rhythm of work and reporting.'],
  'seo-agency-london': ['London search results are some of the most competitive in the UK, so pick an agency that can explain exactly where you can realistically win, borough by borough and topic by topic.', 'Being based in London is not a skill. Judge an agency on its process, reporting, honesty about timelines and how well it understands your buyers.', 'Remote SEO works well for London businesses when there is a clear monthly rhythm, shared reporting and direct access to the people doing the work.'],
  'seo-agency-manchester': ['Manchester businesses often need two SEO plans at once: local visibility across Greater Manchester towns and national reach for ecommerce, digital and B2B services.', 'Ask any agency to show how it would target specific towns and areas such as Salford, Stockport or Trafford without creating thin copy-and-paste location pages.', 'A remote UK agency can deliver the same SEO work as a local one, provided there is a clear plan, regular calls and reporting tied to enquiries and sales.'],
  'ai-overviews-seo-uk': ['AI Overviews draw on pages that already rank and are easy to understand, so strong traditional SEO remains the foundation.', 'Answer questions directly near the top of the page, cover the follow-up questions, and keep facts consistent across your site and the wider web.', 'Measure AI visibility alongside clicks, because an AI Overview can reduce clicks for simple questions even when your brand is cited.'],
  'core-web-vitals-uk': ['Core Web Vitals are three measures of real user experience: Largest Contentful Paint (loading), Interaction to Next Paint (responsiveness) and Cumulative Layout Shift (visual stability).', 'Judge your site on field data from real visitors, not a single lab score, and fix templates rather than individual pages.', 'Core Web Vitals are a modest ranking factor, but faster, steadier pages usually convert better, which is the bigger commercial reason to fix them.'],
  'keyword-research-guide-uk': ['Start from your customers and your offer, not from a tool. Seed terms come from sales calls, enquiries and the words buyers actually use.', 'Group keywords by search intent and map each group to a single page, so you never have two pages competing for the same query.', 'Prioritise by commercial value and realistic difficulty, not volume alone. Low-volume UK long-tail searches often convert best.'],
  'schema-markup-guide-uk': ['Schema markup is structured data that describes your business, pages and products in a format machines can read, usually added as JSON-LD.', 'Only mark up what is visible on the page and true. Markup that does not match the content can lose rich results or trigger a manual action.', 'Self-serving review markup about your own business is not eligible for review rich results, so do not rely on star ratings for your own services.'],
  'seo-reporting-uk': ['A useful SEO report starts with business outcomes such as enquiries, sales and revenue, then explains the search metrics that led to them.', 'Use Google Search Console for search visibility and GA4 for what visitors did next. Neither tells the full story alone.', 'Every report should end with what was done, what was learned and what happens next, not just a page of charts.'],
  'facebook-ads-for-small-business-uk': ['Start with one product or service, one clear offer and one goal, rather than trying to advertise everything at once.', 'Set up the Meta pixel and conversion tracking before you spend, so you can see which ads actually bring sales or enquiries.', 'Plan for several weeks of testing and keep refreshing creative; small budgets go further when the account stays simple.'],
  'google-ads-cost-uk': ['Google Ads has no set price. You choose a daily budget and pay per click, and what each click costs depends on a live auction that changes all the time.', 'Total cost has three parts: ad spend, management, and the landing pages and tracking that make the clicks worth paying for.', 'Work backwards from what a customer is worth to you, then test a modest budget long enough to learn before you scale.'],
  'google-ads-for-small-business-uk': ['Start narrow: a few high-intent keywords, a tight location and one campaign, rather than broad targeting that spends quickly on poor clicks.', 'Set up conversion tracking for calls, forms and sales before launch, so you can tell which searches bring customers.', 'Review search terms and add negative keywords every week; most small-account waste comes from irrelevant searches.'],
  'meta-ads-cost-uk': ['Meta Ads has no fixed price. You set a budget and Meta\'s auction decides what each impression, click or result costs, which shifts with audience, season and creative.', 'Creative is the biggest lever on Meta. Fresh, relevant ads usually do more for cost than fiddling with targeting.', 'Budget for ad spend, management and creative production separately, and judge results on cost per sale or lead, not cost per click.'],
  'remarketing-guide-uk': ['Remarketing reaches people who already know you, such as site visitors, basket abandoners and past customers, so it usually needs a different message from cold ads.', 'Segment audiences by how close people came to buying, and cap frequency so ads help rather than irritate.', 'In the UK, remarketing relies on cookies and customer data, so consent under PECR and UK GDPR must be handled properly.'],
  'ecommerce-seo-checklist': ['Work through ecommerce SEO in order: crawlability first, then category and product pages, then content, links and tracking.', 'Category pages usually carry the most commercial search demand, so they deserve the most attention.', 'Most checks apply to Shopify, WooCommerce and other platforms alike; only the settings you use to fix them differ.'],
  'product-page-seo-uk': ['Unique, specific product descriptions beat copied manufacturer text, both for rankings and for conversion.', 'Accurate product structured data with GBP pricing and availability helps Google show your products well.', 'Handle variants and out-of-stock items deliberately so you avoid thin duplicates and lost rankings.'],
  'shopify-website-cost-uk': ['A Shopify website has two kinds of cost: the one-off build and the ongoing running costs of plan, apps and payments.', 'Our ecommerce builds typically cost £1,500 to £3,500, with Shopify plan, theme and app costs quoted separately because they vary.', 'The biggest price drivers are catalogue size, design complexity, integrations and data migration, not the platform itself.'],
  'woocommerce-seo-uk': ['WooCommerce gives you full control over URLs, templates and schema, but that control means more things can go wrong.', 'Category pages usually win the most valuable searches, so give them unique copy, clean filters and strong internal links.', 'Speed on WooCommerce depends heavily on hosting, theme and plugin choices, so audit them before adding more content.'],
  'wordpress-website-cost-uk': ['A small WordPress business website from Prism Works Studio typically costs £1,000 to £2,000; a WooCommerce shop typically £1,500 to £3,500.', 'Hosting, premium themes and paid plugins are third-party costs that vary, so we quote them separately.', 'WordPress needs regular updates, backups and security checks, so plan for maintenance as well as the build.'],
  'blog-writing-service-uk': ['A good blog writing service does more than write: it researches search demand, plans topics and optimises each post so it can rank and convert.', 'Pricing is usually per post, a monthly retainer or part of a wider content and SEO package; compare what is included, not just the price.', 'Brief well, review for accuracy and judge results on enquiries over 3 to 6 months.'],
  'brand-identity-design-uk': ['Brand identity design is the visual system behind your business: logo, colours, typography, imagery and the rules for using them consistently.', 'Good identity work starts with strategy, so the design reflects who you serve and how you want to be seen.', 'Plan how the identity will roll out across your website, social profiles, ads and print before you sign off the design.'],
  'content-strategy-uk': ['A content strategy is a written plan that links your business goals to the questions your customers ask, so every piece of content has a job to do.', 'Start with audiences, goals and search demand, then build topic clusters and an editorial calendar you can actually keep up with.', 'Judge content on enquiries and sales over 3 to 6 months, and refresh what already ranks before writing more.'],
  'pr-for-small-business-uk': ['PR for a small business is about earning mentions, coverage and links from places your customers trust, not buying adverts.', 'Start with a clear story, a short list of relevant publications and genuinely useful expert commentary or data.', 'Digital PR also supports SEO, because quality links and brand mentions help search engines and AI tools trust your site.'],
  'tone-of-voice-guide-uk': ['A tone of voice guide is a short, practical document that tells anyone writing for your business how it should sound, with examples.', 'Base your voice on your customers and positioning, describe it with a few clear traits and show what each looks like in practice.', 'Your voice stays the same everywhere, but your tone adapts to the situation, such as a sales page, a complaint reply or a social post.'],
  'beauty-salon-marketing-uk': ['Salon clients search locally and judge on photos and reviews, so your Google Business Profile matters most.', 'Make booking effortless: one tap from Instagram, Google or your website to a confirmed appointment.', 'Rebooking and retention fill more of the diary than chasing new clients alone.'],
  'care-home-marketing-uk': ['Families choose care homes carefully, so honest, detailed information builds more trust than slogans.', 'Local search and a clear website do most of the work; paid ads support specific vacancies.', 'Keep claims accurate and inspection references current, with sign-off resting with the provider.'],
  'gym-marketing-uk': ['Most gym members live or work nearby, so local search and a strong Google Business Profile come first.', 'Paid social works best with a clear trial offer, a simple booking page and fast follow-up.', 'Retention is marketing too: keeping members costs less than replacing them.'],
  'recruitment-agency-marketing-uk': ['Marketing for recruitment agencies has two audiences, clients and candidates, so plan separate messages and pages for each.', 'A clear niche gives SEO, content and LinkedIn something specific to say.', 'Track placements and client enquiries by source, not just applications or followers.'],
  'tradesman-marketing-uk': ['Most trade jobs start with a local search, so a strong Google Business Profile and service-area pages come first.', 'Google Ads suit urgent jobs; SEO builds steady enquiries for planned work over time.', 'Answer calls quickly and show proof of work: speed and trust win most trade jobs.'],
  'architect-marketing-uk': ['Clients judge architects on their work, so a fast, well-organised portfolio website is the foundation.', 'SEO for project types and locations helps homeowners and commercial clients find you when they start planning.', 'Case studies, PR and LinkedIn build the credibility that turns interest into appointments.'],
  'multi-location-seo-uk': ['Multi-location SEO gives each branch its own accurate Google Business Profile and genuinely useful location page.', 'A clear site structure, a master list of business details and a repeatable new-branch routine keep data consistent.', 'Report by branch, because a strong average can hide locations that are struggling.'],
  'nursery-marketing-uk': ['Parents choose childcare close to home or work, so local search and Google Business Profile matter most.', 'A warm, honest website and an easy show-round booking turn searches into visits.', 'Children\'s privacy and accurate claims must shape every photo, post and advert.'],
  'vet-practice-marketing-uk': ['Most clients choose a vet close to home, so local search and Google Business Profile come first.', 'A clear, fast website with easy booking and emergency information builds trust before the first visit.', 'Keep claims accurate and check professional guidance, because veterinary marketing carries extra responsibility.'],
  'wedding-business-marketing-uk': ['Couples plan a year or more ahead, so wedding marketing has to work across a long, research-heavy journey.', 'Search, Google Business Profile and a portfolio-led website do the heavy lifting; paid social adds reach at peak planning times.', 'Fast, personal replies to enquiries often decide who gets the booking.'],
  'cleaning-company-marketing-uk': ['Trust is the deciding factor, so reviews, insurance details and real photos matter more than clever slogans.', 'Separate pages for domestic, commercial and specialist cleaning help the right clients find you.', 'Regular clients are where the value is, so make retention part of your marketing plan.'],
  'driving-school-marketing-uk': ['Learners and parents search locally, so Google Business Profile and local SEO usually come first.', 'Clear information on areas covered, lesson types and availability turns visitors into enquiries.', 'Fast, friendly replies to enquiries often matter as much as the marketing itself.'],
  'florist-marketing-uk': ['Florists sell to two audiences at once: urgent local gift buyers and planners booking events.', 'A simple online shop with clear delivery areas and cut-off times can capture last-minute orders.', 'Peak dates need planning weeks in advance, from content to ads to capacity.'],
  'photographer-marketing-uk': ['A fast, focused portfolio website is the centre of a photographer\'s marketing.', 'Clear specialisms and local relevance help the right clients find you in search.', 'Consent, image rights and honest pricing information build trust and reduce wasted enquiries.'],
  'physiotherapy-clinic-marketing-uk': ['Most patients search for a physio near them when they are in pain, so local search and fast booking matter most.', 'Condition and treatment pages written in plain English help patients choose you and help search engines understand you.', 'Healthcare advertising rules and professional standards should shape every claim, review and advert.'],
  'shopify-web-design-london': ['London brands compete UK-wide online, so Shopify store speed, product pages and checkout clarity matter more than location.', 'A well-configured theme with focused custom sections often beats a heavy custom build or a pile of apps.', 'Migrations need redirect planning and thorough testing to protect sales and existing search traffic.'],
  'wix-to-wordpress-migration': ['Wix has no simple one-click export to WordPress, so a migration is really a careful rebuild plus a content move.', 'Redirecting every old URL to its new equivalent is the most important step for protecting search visibility.', 'Plan, build and test on a staging site before switching the domain, then monitor closely after launch.'],
  'wordpress-hosting-uk': ['Hosting affects your WordPress site\'s speed, security and reliability, so the cheapest plan is rarely the best value.', 'Managed WordPress hosting handles more of the technical work, while shared and cloud options trade cost against responsibility.', 'Make sure your business owns the hosting account and that backups, support and server location suit your needs.'],
  'wordpress-page-builders-uk': ['How a WordPress site is built affects its speed, how easy it is to edit and how much maintenance it needs.', 'Page builders offer flexible editing, custom themes offer control and performance, and the block editor sits in between.', 'Choose based on who will edit the site, how often it changes and how important performance and consistency are.'],
  'wordpress-security-uk': ['Most WordPress security problems come from outdated software, weak logins and poorly chosen plugins rather than WordPress itself.', 'Good hosting, regular updates, tested backups and fewer plugins reduce risk more than any single security tool.', 'Have a written plan for what to do if the site is compromised, including who to call and where your backups live.'],
  'wordpress-small-business-website': ['A small business website should be planned around what customers need to know and the action you want them to take.', 'WordPress is flexible and widely supported, but it needs hosting, updates and care to stay fast and secure.', 'Clear service pages, trust signals, simple contact routes and basic SEO matter more than complex features.'],
  'shopify-conversion-rate-optimisation': ['Shopify CRO starts with data: find where shoppers drop off before changing anything.', 'Clear product pages, honest delivery information and a smooth cart usually matter more than clever tricks.', 'Test meaningful changes and measure revenue, not just clicks.'],
  'shopify-speed-optimisation': ['Unused apps, heavy images and third-party scripts are among the most common causes of slow Shopify stores.', 'Measure real-user performance and Core Web Vitals before and after changes, not just a single test score.', 'Speed work should protect conversion features, so test changes rather than stripping things out blindly.'],
  'shopify-store-setup-uk': ['Get core settings right first: business details, currency, VAT, shipping and payments.', 'Clear product pages, delivery information and legal policies build trust with UK shoppers.', 'Set up analytics, SEO basics and test orders before you announce your launch.'],
  'shopify-theme-customisation': ['Much can be achieved in the Shopify theme editor before any custom code is needed.', 'Custom sections and blocks let your team keep editing content without a developer.', 'Always work on a duplicate theme, keep backups and test speed and mobile layout before publishing.'],
  'woocommerce-to-shopify-migration': ['A WooCommerce to Shopify migration is mainly a data, design and SEO project, not just a platform switch.', 'Mapping every old URL to a new one with permanent redirects is the most important step for protecting rankings.', 'Test orders, payments, tax, shipping and emails thoroughly before you point your domain at Shopify.'],
  'web-design-birmingham': ['Birmingham and West Midlands manufacturers sell to engineers and buyers, who want detail, not slogans.', 'Capability pages, sector pages and a well-designed quote form usually generate more leads than a striking home page.', 'A B2B website should make it easy for sales teams to see which pages and enquiries lead to real orders.'],
  'web-design-glasgow': ['Glasgow tourism businesses design for visitors who do not know the city, so clear information and easy booking come first.', 'Local service businesses win on trust and convenience: areas covered, real reviews and quick contact options.', 'Both should make their website and Google Business Profile tell the same accurate story.'],
  'web-design-liverpool': ['Liverpool logistics and maritime firms need websites that explain services, routes and capabilities clearly to business buyers.', 'Creative studios need portfolio sites that show their work beautifully without becoming slow.', 'Both benefit from fast pages, clear enquiry routes and content their own team can update.'],
  'web-design-london': ['Most London professional firms already have a website, so the real job is a careful redesign rather than a fresh start.', 'Clients choose advisers on trust, so clear expertise pages, real people and plain language matter more than visual trends.', 'Redirect planning and content audits protect the search visibility a firm has already built.'],
  'web-design-manchester': ['Manchester startups usually benefit from launching a lean, focused site quickly and improving it based on real feedback.', 'Hospitality websites live on phones, so menus, bookings, opening hours and directions must work in seconds.', 'Both groups need a site their own team can update without waiting for a developer.'],
  'ecommerce-website-design-uk': ['Ecommerce design is about helping shoppers find, judge and buy products with as little friction as possible.', 'Product pages and checkout usually matter more than the home page.', 'UK shoppers expect clear delivery costs, returns information and familiar payment options.'],
  'small-business-website-checklist': ['Make sure the business owns its domain, hosting account and content from day one.', 'A short list of essential pages, done well, beats a large site full of thin content.', 'Check forms, tracking and mobile layout before launch, then keep reviewing after.'],
  'website-accessibility-uk': ['Accessibility means people can use your site whatever their sight, hearing, movement or way of reading.', 'WCAG is the widely used technical standard; most businesses aim for its AA level.', 'Many common problems, such as poor contrast, missing alt text and unlabelled forms, are straightforward to fix.'],
  'website-builder-vs-custom-website': ['Hosted builders trade flexibility for simplicity; self-hosted and custom sites trade simplicity for control.', 'The right choice depends on what the site must do in two or three years, not just at launch.', 'Whatever you choose, make sure you can export your content and keep your domain.'],
  'website-copywriting-uk': ['Good website copy starts with the visitor\'s problem, not the business\'s history.', 'Each page should have one main job and one obvious next step.', 'Specific, honest wording builds more trust than superlatives you cannot back up.'],
  'ecommerce-product-photography': ['Ecommerce photography should answer what a shopper would otherwise check in person: size, texture, detail and use.', 'A consistent style across the catalogue makes a store easier to browse and compare.', 'Decide what to shoot in-house or commission, then size, compress and describe images properly for the web.'],
  'headless-commerce-explained': ['Headless commerce separates the customer-facing storefront from the system that handles products, carts and orders.', 'It offers design freedom and flexibility across channels, but adds build cost, technical complexity and ongoing maintenance.', 'Most small and mid-sized UK stores are better served by a well-built theme; headless suits brands with specific needs a theme cannot meet.'],
  'shopify-vs-squarespace-uk': ['Shopify is built around selling; Squarespace is built around presenting a brand, with selling added on.', 'If products are the heart of the business and you expect to grow the catalogue, Shopify is usually the safer long-term choice.', 'If you mainly sell services, bookings or a handful of products alongside a content-led site, Squarespace can be simpler to run.'],
  'website-contact-forms': ['Ask only for what you need to respond well; every extra field gives people a reason to give up.', 'Tell visitors what happens after they press send, and make the button say what it does.', 'A form is only as good as the follow-up: route enquiries quickly and test the whole journey regularly.'],
  'website-discovery-workshop': ['A discovery workshop is a structured conversation that agrees goals, audience, content and scope before design or build begins.', 'Its value is in surfacing assumptions and disagreements early, when changing direction is cheap.', 'You get more from it by preparing data, examples and decisions in advance and bringing the people who will sign off.'],
  'business-domain-and-email-setup': ['Register your domain in the business\'s own account and keep access details safe; losing control of a domain is painful to fix.', 'Use email addresses on your own domain rather than free webmail addresses for a more professional, portable setup.', 'Set up SPF, DKIM and DMARC records so your emails are less likely to be marked as spam or spoofed.'],
  'ecommerce-category-page-design': ['Category pages are where most shoppers narrow down their choice, so they deserve as much care as product pages.', 'Useful filters, honest sorting and consistent product cards do more for conversion than decoration.', 'Category pages can rank well for broad searches, but filter combinations need managing so they do not create endless duplicate URLs.'],
  'mobile-website-design': ['Design for the phone first, then expand for larger screens, rather than squeezing a desktop design down.', 'Speed, readable text and easy-to-tap controls matter more on mobile than decorative detail.', 'Test on real devices and real connections, not only by resizing a desktop browser.'],
  'website-homepage-design': ['A homepage is a signpost, not a brochure: it should tell visitors what you do, who it is for and where to go next.', 'The opening screen matters most, so lead with a plain statement of what you offer rather than a slogan.', 'Build the page from your visitors\' questions in the order they ask them, then cut anything that does not help.'],
  'website-navigation-structure': ['Organise pages around how customers think about what you offer, not around your internal departments.', 'Use plain, specific menu labels and keep the main menu short; the footer and inner pages can carry the rest.', 'A clear structure helps visitors and search engines alike, so plan it before design, not after.'],
  'about-us-page-writing': ['A good about page is really about your customer: why you are the right people to help them.', 'Honest specifics, such as how you work, who you serve and real photos, are more persuasive than generic mission statements.', 'End with a clear next step so interested visitors know what to do.'],
  'ecommerce-site-search': ['Shoppers who use site search often know what they want, so a poor search experience can lose otherwise easy sales.', 'Good search handles misspellings, synonyms and product attributes, and never leaves a shopper at a dead end.', 'Search terms are a valuable source of insight into what customers want and the words they use.'],
  'service-page-design': ['Each main service usually deserves its own page, so you can explain it properly and appear for relevant searches.', 'A strong service page answers what it is, who it is for, how it works, why you and what to do next.', 'Clear structure, genuine proof and an obvious call to action matter more than elaborate design.'],
  'website-image-optimisation': ['Images are often among the largest files on a page, so optimising them is one of the simplest ways to improve speed.', 'Resize images to the dimensions they are displayed at, choose a suitable format and compress them sensibly.', 'Descriptive alt text and file names help accessibility and image search, alongside speed.'],
  'website-trust-signals': ['Trust signals are the details that help a visitor decide your business is real, competent and safe to deal with.', 'The strongest signals are honest and verifiable: clear contact details, genuine reviews, transparent policies and real photos.', 'Invented testimonials, fake badges or exaggerated claims can backfire and may breach consumer protection rules.'],
  'ecommerce-delivery-and-returns-pages': ['Shoppers often check delivery and returns before they buy, so unclear information can stop a purchase.', 'State options, costs, timescales and conditions plainly, and show key points on product, basket and checkout pages too.', 'Returns information must reflect consumer law and your own terms accurately, so check it carefully and keep it current.'],
  'ecommerce-product-descriptions': ['A good product description answers the questions a shopper would ask if they could hold the product or speak to someone in a shop.', 'Lead with what the product does for the customer, then back it up with clear, accurate specifications.', 'Original descriptions written for your own customers are more useful, and more distinctive, than copy pasted from a supplier.'],
  'website-colour-and-typography': ['A small, deliberate set of colours and fonts makes a website look more professional than a wide variety.', 'Readability and contrast come first; a colour or font that looks striking but is hard to read works against you.', 'Defining colours and type as a simple system makes the site consistent and easier to maintain.'],
  'website-faq-page': ['A useful FAQ page answers the questions real customers ask, not questions the business wishes they would ask.', 'Short, direct answers with links to fuller information work better than long, defensive explanations.', 'FAQs belong wherever the question arises, so a central FAQ page should support, not replace, answers on key pages.'],
  'website-footer-design': ['The footer is where visitors look when they cannot find something elsewhere, so it should act as a reliable safety net.', 'Group footer links into a few clear sections rather than listing every page on the site.', 'Contact details, legal information and key policies belong in the footer, presented clearly on every screen size.'],
  '404-page-design': ['A good 404 page explains what happened in plain language and gives visitors useful routes onwards.', 'The page should return a genuine 404 status code, not redirect everything to the homepage.', 'Regularly finding and fixing the broken links that cause 404s matters more than the design of the page itself.'],
  'ecommerce-product-variants-and-bundles': ['Use variants for versions of the same product and separate products when items differ meaningfully or are searched for in their own right.', 'Every variant needs clear names, accurate stock and, ideally, its own image so customers know exactly what they are buying.', 'Bundles should solve a real customer need, with transparent pricing and stock that stays in sync with the individual items.'],
  'ecommerce-subscriptions-uk': ['Subscriptions work best for products people genuinely run out of or want to receive regularly, not as a bolt-on for everything.', 'Make the subscription easy to understand, easy to manage and easy to cancel; trust is what keeps subscribers paying.', 'Plan the operational side, such as stock, failed payments and dispatch dates, before you launch the offer.'],
  'selling-internationally-uk-online-store': ['Start with one or two markets where you already see interest, rather than switching on every country at once.', 'Be upfront about total costs, including delivery, duties and taxes, so overseas customers are not surprised at the door.', 'Tax and customs rules are complex and change, so take professional advice before you sell cross-border.'],
  'website-testimonials-page': ['Specific, attributable testimonials from real customers are far more persuasive than vague praise.', 'Ask at the right moment, make it easy and always get permission to publish names and details.', 'Never invent, edit the meaning of or selectively hide feedback; honesty is both a legal requirement and the whole point.'],
  'ecommerce-customer-accounts-and-wishlists': ['Customer accounts should make repeat buying and after-sales tasks easier, never stand in the way of a first purchase.', 'Order history, tracking, returns and saved addresses are the features most account holders actually need.', 'Wishlists work best when they are easy to use without friction and connect sensibly to stock and email updates.'],
  'ecommerce-gift-cards-and-vouchers': ['Gift cards are a product in their own right and deserve a clear, well-designed product page.', 'Delivery, redemption and balance checking should be simple for both the buyer and the recipient.', 'Expiry, VAT treatment and fraud controls need careful thought, and legal and tax points should be checked with an adviser.'],
  'ecommerce-product-reviews': ['Genuine product reviews help shoppers decide and give you useful feedback, but only if they are honest and easy to find.', 'Asking at the right time, after the product has arrived and been used, tends to produce more helpful reviews.', 'Fake or selectively hidden reviews can mislead customers, and UK consumer law treats this seriously.'],
  'ecommerce-stock-availability-display': ['Clear, accurate stock information reduces disappointment, customer service queries and cancelled orders.', 'Out-of-stock products usually deserve a helpful page rather than deletion, especially if they will return.', 'Low-stock messages should always reflect real inventory; false urgency damages trust and may breach consumer rules.'],
  'website-pop-ups-done-well': ['A pop-up should offer something genuinely useful at a moment that makes sense for the visitor.', 'Timing, frequency and easy dismissal matter more than flashy design.', 'On mobile, intrusive overlays can frustrate visitors and may work against your search visibility, so keep them small and polite.'],
  'cookie-banner-design-uk': ['UK rules generally expect consent before non-essential cookies are set, and accepting and rejecting should be equally easy.', 'A good banner is short, plainly worded, works on mobile and does not block the content people came for longer than needed.', 'Check that the banner actually controls what loads: a banner that looks right but sets tracking cookies anyway is the most common failure.'],
  'ecommerce-size-guides': ['Customers buying clothing, footwear and many other products online need to judge fit without trying anything on; a clear size guide fills that gap.', 'Use real garment or product measurements, explain how to measure, and add fit notes that describe how items actually wear.', 'Put size help right beside the size selector, make it work on mobile and keep it specific to the product where fit varies.'],
  'ecommerce-transactional-emails': ['Transactional emails are triggered by something a customer did, such as placing an order, and they are among the most opened messages a shop sends.', 'Each email should answer the customer\'s likely question at that moment: what did I order, when will it arrive, what happens next.', 'Keep them clearly service-led; heavy marketing content in transactional emails can raise consent questions and reduce trust.'],
  'website-online-booking-systems': ['Online booking suits services with fixed durations and clear prices; complex or quoted work often still needs an enquiry form.', 'The booking flow should ask for as little as possible, show availability clearly and confirm instantly.', 'Integrate booking into your site design and service pages rather than sending people to a disconnected page.'],
  'website-staging-and-testing': ['A staging site is a private copy of your website where changes can be built and tested without affecting real visitors.', 'Testing should cover what customers do, not just how pages look: forms, checkout, emails, mobile, speed and tracking.', 'Staging stays useful after launch for testing updates, plugins and theme changes before they reach the live site.'],
  'ecommerce-loyalty-programmes': ['A loyalty programme rewards customers for coming back, but only works if the rewards matter to them and the costs suit your margins.', 'Points, tiers, paid memberships and non-discount perks each suit different kinds of store.', 'Clear rules, simple wording and honest terms keep a programme trusted and easier to manage.'],
  'ecommerce-pre-launch-marketing': ['Pre-launch marketing gives a new store an audience on day one rather than starting from nothing.', 'A coming soon page with an email sign-up is often the simplest foundation to build on.', 'SEO, analytics and tracking groundwork done before launch saves rework and lets you measure results from the start.'],
  'website-content-audit': ['A content audit is a structured review of every page to decide whether it should be kept, improved, merged or removed.', 'Judge pages on usefulness, accuracy and purpose as well as traffic, since some low-traffic pages still matter.', 'Merging and removing pages needs care with redirects so visitors and search engines are not sent to dead ends.'],
  'website-live-chat-vs-chatbot': ['Live chat is staffed by people; chatbots answer automatically. Many sites use a mix of both.', 'Chat only helps if it is answered promptly or clearly explains when a reply will come.', 'Good FAQ content, clear contact options and honest handover to a person matter more than the tool itself.'],
  'website-video-guide': ['Video helps when it shows something words and photos cannot, such as a product in use or a process explained.', 'Background and autoplay videos are the most likely to slow pages down and distract visitors, so use them sparingly.', 'Lazy loading, compressed files, poster images and captions keep video fast, accessible and useful.'],
  'ecommerce-packaging-and-unboxing': ['Packaging has to protect the product first; presentation and branding come after that.', 'Size, weight and materials affect delivery costs, damage rates and how customers feel about your brand\'s environmental impact.', 'The unboxing moment connects back to your website through inserts, care information and easy routes to reviews, reorders and returns.'],
  'ecommerce-product-comparison-pages': ['Comparison content helps shoppers who are stuck between similar products, which can reduce hesitation and returns.', 'Choose the right format: a static comparison table, an interactive compare tool or an editorial guide each suit different ranges.', 'Compare attributes that matter to the decision, keep data accurate and consistent, and stay fair and factual.'],
  'ecommerce-seasonal-sales-preparation': ['Seasonal preparation works best when it starts well ahead of the busy period, leaving time to build, test and fix.', 'Seasonal collections, gift guides and clear delivery information help shoppers find the right products and buy in time.', 'Offers must be genuine and clearly explained, and the site needs to cope with extra traffic and orders.'],
  'website-hero-section-design': ['The hero section is the first thing visitors see, so its main job is to make clear what you offer and who it is for.', 'A specific headline, a supporting line, one primary call to action and relevant imagery usually do more than sliders or vague slogans.', 'Design the hero for mobile and for page speed from the start, then test changes rather than guessing.'],
  'website-pricing-page-design': ['A pricing page helps visitors work out whether you are a realistic fit, which can save time on both sides.', 'Choose a format that suits how you actually price: fixed packages, starting prices, ranges or quote-based pricing.', 'Be clear about what is and is not included, show prices honestly and answer common questions on the page.'],
  'food-and-drink-ecommerce-uk': ['Food and drink stores carry extra responsibilities online, including clear allergen and product information before purchase.', 'Delivery is a core part of the product: packaging, courier choice, delivery days and shelf life shape what you can sell and where.', 'Consumable products suit repeat orders and subscriptions, so plan for returning customers from the start.'],
  'shopify-clothing-brand-uk': ['Clothing stores depend on navigation, variants, sizing information and imagery more than most other product types.', 'Plan how products, colours and sizes are structured before you build, because it affects filters, stock, search and reporting.', 'Returns are part of selling clothes online, so a clear policy and good fit information protect both margins and customer trust.'],
  'squarespace-vs-wordpress-uk': ['Squarespace is an all-in-one hosted builder that trades flexibility for simplicity, while WordPress gives far more control in exchange for more responsibility.', 'Both can rank well in Google; content, structure and speed matter more than the platform name.', 'Choose based on how your site needs to grow, who will maintain it and how much control over code, data and hosting you want.'],
  'therapist-website-design-uk': ['A therapist\'s website should help a nervous visitor feel understood, see clearly how you work and know exactly how to make contact.', 'Plain language, honest descriptions of your approach and visible professional details build more trust than polished marketing copy.', 'Contact forms and booking tools handle sensitive information, so privacy, security and data protection need care from the start.'],
  'wix-vs-shopify-uk': ['Shopify is built around selling products, while Wix is a general website builder with ecommerce added to it.', 'Wix often suits service businesses and small catalogues; Shopify usually suits businesses where online sales are the main source of revenue.', 'Think about where you expect to be in two or three years, because moving platform later usually means a rebuild.'],
  'bigcommerce-vs-shopify-uk': ['Shopify and BigCommerce are both hosted ecommerce platforms, so the choice is about fit rather than one being simply better.', 'BigCommerce leans towards more built-in features; Shopify leans towards a very large app and theme ecosystem.', 'Catalogue complexity, B2B needs, integrations and who will run the store day to day are usually the deciding factors.'],
  'shopify-beauty-skincare-brand-uk': ['Beauty shoppers want ingredients, usage guidance and honest results information, so product pages need to do more than look good.', 'Cosmetic claims and product information are regulated in the UK, so check wording carefully and take advice where needed.', 'Replenishment, bundles and routines suit Shopify well and can encourage repeat purchases when planned around real customer needs.'],
  'shopify-furniture-homeware-uk': ['Furniture and homeware shoppers need precise dimensions, materials and imagery to picture a product in their home.', 'Large items bring delivery, lead time and returns challenges that should be designed into the store rather than added later.', 'Configurable products such as fabric, finish and size options need careful planning to work well within Shopify.'],
  'shopify-jewellery-brand-uk': ['Jewellery is bought on trust and detail, so imagery, scale, materials and policies need to answer questions a shopper would ask in person.', 'Plan how metals, stone options, sizes and personalisation are structured before building, because Shopify\'s variant model shapes everything else.', 'Gifting, hallmarking information and clear returns rules for personalised pieces are specific to jewellery and worth getting right early.'],
  'wix-vs-wordpress-uk': ['Wix is a hosted, all-in-one builder that trades flexibility for convenience; WordPress is open-source software that trades convenience for control.', 'The right choice depends on who will run the site, how much it needs to grow and how much maintenance you are prepared to take on.', 'Moving from one to the other is possible but rarely automatic, so it is worth choosing with the next few years in mind.'],
  'etsy-to-shopify-migration': ['Etsy brings marketplace traffic; your own Shopify store brings control over branding, customer relationships and presentation, but you must drive visitors yourself.', 'Many sellers run both for a period, keeping Etsy sales going while the Shopify store builds an audience.', 'Moving products is the easy part; building traffic, writing your own policies and earning trust take the most planning.'],
  'shopify-art-print-sellers-uk': ['Originals, limited editions and open editions behave differently in stock and pricing, so model them deliberately in Shopify.', 'Size and framing options are the main variants for prints, and shoppers need help picturing scale on a wall.', 'Your own Shopify store gives more control over presentation and customer relationships than a marketplace, alongside the extra work of driving traffic.'],
  'shopify-pet-products-brand-uk': ['Pet shoppers browse by animal, size and life stage, so the catalogue structure should mirror how owners think about their pets.', 'Pet food, treats and some health products carry UK labelling and claims rules, so check current guidance before writing product copy.', 'Repeat purchases such as food, litter and treats make subscriptions and easy reordering worth planning from the start.'],
  'shopify-pos-uk-retail': ['Shopify POS lets a physical shop and an online store share one product catalogue, stock count and customer record.', 'Click and collect, in-store returns of online orders and ordering out-of-stock items for delivery are where a joined-up setup helps most.', 'Check hardware, card reader availability, plan features and integrations against how your shop actually trades before committing.'],
  'shopify-supplements-brand-uk': ['Food supplements are regulated in the UK, and health claims in particular are tightly controlled, so product copy needs careful checking.', 'Shopify can run a supplement store well, but some payment providers and ad platforms apply extra restrictions to this category.', 'Clear ingredient, dosage and warning information on every product page builds trust and supports compliance.'],
  'coach-website-design-uk': ['A coaching website works best when it speaks directly to a specific person and the change they are looking for.', 'Clear packages, an easy discovery call route and honest descriptions of what coaching can and cannot do build trust.', 'Claims about outcomes need care, and booking, payment and privacy tools should be set up properly from the start.'],
  'consultant-website-design-uk': ['A consultant\'s website should make it obvious who you help, what problem you solve and what working with you looks like.', 'Specific, honest proof such as approach, credentials and permitted case studies builds more trust than broad claims.', 'A simple, low-pressure enquiry route and a few genuinely useful articles often matter more than a large, complex site.'],
  'shopify-candle-home-fragrance-uk': ['Scent cannot be experienced online, so product pages need careful descriptions, consistent scent notes and supporting tools such as samples.', 'Candles and fragrance products can carry safety labelling obligations, so check current requirements with official guidance and a specialist.', 'Well-structured variants, sensible shipping for fragile items and repeat purchase features suit this category.'],
  'shopify-gift-stationery-brand-uk': ['Gift and stationery shoppers often browse by occasion, recipient or budget, so navigation should support those journeys.', 'Personalisation, multi-buy offers, low-value postage and wholesale all need careful setup to keep orders accurate and profitable.', 'Seasonal peaks around Christmas, Valentine\'s Day and Mother\'s Day shape the year, so planning ahead matters.'],
  'tutoring-business-website-uk': ['A tutoring website usually has two audiences, parents and students, and needs to reassure the person paying while speaking to the person learning.', 'Clear subjects, levels, formats, tutor details and practical information help families decide quickly.', 'Safeguarding information, children\'s data and payment terms need care, and regulatory points should be checked with official guidance.'],
  'construction-company-website-design-uk': ['A construction website needs to show the type of work you do, where you do it and evidence that you do it well.', 'Accurate project case studies, genuine accreditations and a clear quote request route help both homeowners and commercial clients judge fit.', 'Claims about accreditations, insurance, guarantees and compliance should be specific, current and supportable.'],
  'interior-designer-website-design-uk': ['An interior design website is largely judged on its portfolio, so project pages need strong images and enough context to explain the work.', 'Clearly described services, a plain explanation of how you work and a well-designed enquiry form help the right clients get in touch.', 'Image permissions, client privacy and honest descriptions of credentials and projects need care on every page.'],
  'personal-trainer-website-design-uk': ['A personal trainer\'s website works best when it speaks to a specific type of client and makes booking a first session simple.', 'Clear packages, honest descriptions of qualifications and responsible wording about results build trust with people who may be nervous about starting.', 'Health information collected through forms needs particular care under UK GDPR, and results claims need to be realistic and supportable.'],
  'shopify-childrens-products-brand-uk': ['Parents and gift buyers want clear, accurate safety and age information before they buy anything for a child.', 'Product pages, sizing, gifting options and delivery details matter as much as attractive photography for a children\'s brand.', 'Product safety and labelling rules are complex, so check them with the relevant UK guidance or a specialist rather than relying on your website platform.'],
  'shopify-cycling-outdoor-brand-uk': ['Cycling and outdoor buyers often research carefully, so detailed specifications, fit guidance and compatibility information are central to the store.', 'Large or high-value items such as bikes raise practical questions about delivery, assembly, finance and returns that the site should answer clearly.', 'Useful content about choosing, fitting and caring for kit can help buyers decide and support visibility in search.'],
  'cafe-website-design-uk': ['Most cafe website visitors want a few facts fast: where you are, when you are open and what you serve.', 'A text-based menu, accurate hours and a clear map link do more work than elaborate animation.', 'Extras such as pre-ordering, bean sales or event bookings are worth adding only if you can run them day to day.'],
  'cleaning-company-website-design-uk': ['Domestic and commercial cleaning buyers want different things, so give each its own route through the site.', 'A quote form that asks about property size, frequency and access lets you price accurately without a site visit for every enquiry.', 'Trust matters because cleaners work in homes and premises, so explain vetting, insurance and key handling honestly.'],
  'driving-instructor-website-design-uk': ['An independent instructor\'s website should make it obvious which areas you cover, whether you have space and how to enquire.', 'Learners and the parents who often pay for lessons look for different reassurance, so the site should speak to both.', 'Keep claims about qualifications and pass rates accurate and checkable, and avoid anything you cannot back up.'],
  'electrician-website-design-uk': ['An electrician\'s website should separate urgent call-outs from planned work, because the two visitors behave very differently.', 'Registration and certification details are central to trust in electrical work, but describe them accurately and only if you hold them.', 'Service pages and a quote form that captures the right details help you filter jobs before you spend time on site visits.'],
  'hair-salon-barber-website-design-uk': ['For most salons and barbers the website\'s main job is getting a booking made with as few taps as possible.', 'A clear service list, honest duration and price guidance, and real photos of your own work build confidence.', 'Barbers relying on walk-ins need different information up front from appointment-only salons.'],
  'dog-groomer-website-design-uk': ['For most groomers, the website\'s core job is to make booking simple and reduce no-shows and back-and-forth messages.', 'Owners worry about how their dog will be treated, so photos of your space, clear handling policies and honest information about anxious dogs build trust.', 'Services and prices often depend on breed, size and coat condition, and the site should explain that rather than hide it.'],
  'landscaper-website-design-uk': ['Landscaping and garden maintenance attract different customers, so the website should give each its own clear path.', 'A portfolio organised by project, with before and after photos and short stories, does more than a long gallery of loose images.', 'Seasonal changes in demand mean the site should be easy to update, from spring design enquiries to autumn tidy-ups and winter planning.'],
  'plumber-website-design-uk': ['A plumbing website usually serves three very different jobs at once: water emergencies, heating and boiler work, and planned installs like bathrooms.', 'Gas work in the UK must be carried out by someone on the Gas Safe Register, so only promote boiler and gas services you are legally able to do and describe registration accurately.', 'Seasonal demand for heating work means your site should make it easy to update messaging and availability without a rebuild.'],
  'removals-company-website-design-uk': ['A removals website is mostly a quote-gathering tool, so the quote or survey form deserves more design attention than any other part of the site.', 'Moving customers are often stressed and comparing several firms, so clear explanations of what is and is not included build confidence.', 'Insurance, liability and storage terms should be described carefully and accurately, with full details in written terms rather than marketing copy.'],
  'roofer-website-design-uk': ['Customers usually cannot see the roof problem or the finished work themselves, so clear photos and plain explanations do much of the selling.', 'Separate pages for repairs, flat roofs, pitched roofs and chimneys or guttering help visitors find the right service and help search engines understand what you do.', 'Guarantees, insurance and trade body membership should only be shown where you genuinely hold them, described exactly as they apply.'],
  'car-garage-website-design-uk': ['Garage visitors usually want one of three things: to book an MOT, to book a service, or to get a fault looked at, so make each path obvious.', 'Customers are booking a drop-off rather than a visit to their home, so opening hours, location, parking and how to get to work matter more than for most trades.', 'Only describe MOT testing if you are an authorised test centre, and avoid promising fixed repair prices before the car has been inspected.'],
  'kitchen-bathroom-fitter-website-design-uk': ['A kitchen or bathroom is a considered purchase, so the website has to support weeks of research rather than a single urgent phone call.', 'Be clear about whether you supply and fit, fit only, or design as well, because visitors often arrive unsure which kind of firm they need.', 'Gas, electrical and some building work carries regulatory requirements, so describe who carries out each trade and only claim registrations you actually hold.'],
  'locksmith-website-design-uk': ['Locksmith customers are often locked out and wary of being overcharged, so clear pricing explanations and a genuine local identity matter enormously.', 'Locksmithing is not a licensed trade in most of the UK, so describe training, vetting and insurance accurately and avoid implying official approval you do not have.', 'Separate emergency lockout pages from planned security work such as lock upgrades, so each visitor finds the right information quickly.'],
  'solar-panel-installer-website-design-uk': ['Solar customers are often wary of overpromising, so cautious, specific and verifiable wording tends to build more trust than bold claims.', 'Avoid quoting fixed savings, payback periods or export earnings as facts; explain the factors involved and offer a personalised assessment instead.', 'Only claim certifications, consumer code membership or scheme eligibility you can evidence, and point to official sources for schemes and grants.'],
  'window-door-installer-website-design-uk': ['Window and door sites sit between a product catalogue and a trade website, so structure pages around both product types and the installation service.', 'Replacement windows in England and Wales generally need building regulations compliance, often shown through a competent person scheme, so explain this accurately and only claim memberships you hold.', 'Quote forms work best when they ask for the number and type of openings rather than exact measurements the customer cannot reliably take.'],
  'cctv-security-installer-website-design-uk': ['Security customers are often anxious, sometimes after a break-in, so the website should explain options calmly and make a survey easy to request.', 'Give CCTV, alarms, access control and smart security their own pages, and separate home and business customers.', 'Hedge any points about privacy law, police response and insurance, and describe certifications and approvals exactly as they are.'],
  'painter-decorator-website-design-uk': ['Painting and decorating is judged on finish, so a well-organised portfolio of your own before-and-after photos is usually the most persuasive part of the site.', 'Help people describe the job in a quote form, with room types, surfaces, condition and photos, so you can give a realistic estimate.', 'Explain preparation, timescales and what happens in an occupied home honestly, without promising results or durations you cannot guarantee.'],
  'pest-control-website-design-uk': ['Most pest control visitors search for the pest, not the service, so a page for each pest you treat often does more work than a single generic services page.', 'Discretion matters: many householders and businesses are embarrassed about an infestation, so explain unmarked visits or quiet arrival only if you genuinely offer them.', 'Keep claims about chemicals, safety and regulation accurate and hedged, and separate domestic call-outs from commercial contract work.'],
  'scaffolding-company-website-design-uk': ['Scaffolders serve builders, roofers and contractors as well as homeowners, so the website should give trade and domestic visitors their own clear routes.', 'A quote form that asks for the right details, such as property type, height, access and duration, saves time on both sides.', 'Describe training, insurance and safety practice accurately, and hedge points about permits and regulations rather than stating them as fixed rules.'],
  'skip-hire-website-design-uk': ['Skip hire customers mostly want to know which size they need, whether you deliver to their postcode, the price and when it can arrive, so put those answers up front.', 'Online ordering can suit skip hire well, but only if postcode coverage, availability and permit needs are handled properly in the checkout.', 'Explain what can and cannot go in a skip and how permits work in hedged, general terms, since waste rules and council requirements vary.'],
  'care-home-website-design-uk': ['Care home websites are usually read by worried family members making a big decision, often quickly, so clarity and warmth matter more than flashy design.', 'Showing your current inspection rating accurately, explaining care types and being as open as you can about fees all help families shortlist with confidence.', 'Real photos of rooms, communal spaces, gardens and daily life do far more to reassure people than stock images.'],
  'gym-website-design-uk': ['Most gym website visitors want three things quickly: what memberships cost, what the timetable looks like and how to join or try it out.', 'Many potential members feel nervous about walking into a gym for the first time, so showing the space, the people and what a first visit involves can make a real difference.', 'Membership terms should be clear and easy to read before someone signs up, including contract length and how to cancel.'],
  'nursery-website-design-uk': ['Parents choosing a nursery want to know their child will be safe, happy and learning, so the website should show the rooms, the team and a typical day honestly.', 'Funded hours and fees are confusing for many parents, so clear, carefully worded information about what you offer saves time for everyone.', 'Booking a visit or joining a waiting list should be easy to find on every page, especially on mobile.'],
  'optician-website-design-uk': ['For most independent opticians, the website\'s main job is to make booking an eye test simple and to explain what happens at the appointment.', 'Patients often want to know whether they qualify for an NHS-funded sight test, so explaining eligibility in plain terms, and pointing to official guidance, is genuinely useful.', 'Frames are a big part of the choice for many people, so good photography of your range and brands you stock can help a practice stand apart from larger chains.'],
  'vet-practice-website-design-uk': ['Emergency and out-of-hours information should be the easiest thing to find on a vet website, on every page and especially on mobile.', 'New client registration, appointment booking and repeat prescription requests are the everyday tasks the site can take off the phone line.', 'Pet owners choose a vet partly on trust, so honest team profiles, clear fees information and photos of the practice help more than polished slogans.'],
  'accountant-website-design-uk': ['Prospective clients usually want to know quickly whether an accountant works with businesses like theirs, what it might cost and how to get started.', 'Organising services by client type, such as sole traders, limited companies or landlords, often makes a practice site easier to navigate than a list of technical services.', 'Professional body membership, regulatory status and data handling need to be described accurately, so check the rules that apply to your practice.'],
  'estate-agent-website-design-uk': ['An estate agent website serves several audiences at once: buyers, tenants, sellers and landlords, and each needs a clear route through the site.', 'Property portals handle much of the searching, so an agent\'s own site often earns its keep by winning valuations and instructions.', 'Listing feeds, material information and fee disclosure have practical and regulatory implications, so plan them carefully and check current guidance.'],
  'funeral-director-website-design-uk': ['People visiting a funeral director\'s website are often grieving, stressed and short of time, so clarity and calm matter more than anything else.', 'Explaining what to do first, how to reach you at any hour and what things cost can remove a great deal of uncertainty.', 'Funeral directors in the UK are subject to price transparency requirements, so pricing information needs careful planning and checking against current rules.'],
  'hotel-bed-and-breakfast-website-design-uk': ['A hotel or B&B website has one main job: help a guest picture their stay, check availability and book without friction.', 'Room pages, honest photography, clear policies and a well-placed booking button usually matter more than elaborate design effects.', 'The site works best when it is built around how guests actually decide: dates, price, room type, location and reassurance.'],
  'solicitor-website-design-uk': ['People looking for a solicitor are often anxious and unfamiliar with legal processes, so clear, plain-English pages for each practice area matter.', 'Solicitors regulated in England and Wales have transparency obligations covering price and service information for certain services, so plan these pages carefully and check current SRA guidance.', 'Enquiry forms and contact routes should be simple, secure and honest about what happens next.'],
  'charity-website-design-uk': ['A charity website serves several audiences at once, including donors, volunteers, service users and funders, so navigation should give each a clear route.', 'Donation pages should be short, secure and honest, with Gift Aid declarations worded in line with HMRC guidance.', 'Show your registered charity number where required and describe impact accurately, using figures you can evidence.'],
  'dentist-website-design-uk': ['Dental websites should make it immediately clear whether the practice takes NHS patients, private patients or both, and how to register.', 'Treatment pages should explain what is involved in plain language without promising outcomes, in line with GDC standards and advertising rules.', 'Emergency information, opening hours and online booking are among the most-used features, so keep them prominent and accurate.'],
  'holiday-let-website-design-uk': ['A holiday let website works best when each property has its own detailed page with honest photos, sleeping arrangements, accessibility notes and a live availability view.', 'Direct booking only helps if the calendar is reliable, so keep availability synced with any listing platforms you also use to avoid double bookings.', 'Pet, cancellation, deposit and payment terms should be written clearly and checked against your own policies and consumer law, ideally with professional advice.'],
  'recruitment-agency-website-design-uk': ['A recruitment agency website serves two audiences, candidates and hiring clients, so give each a clear, separate route from the home page.', 'Job listings should be easy to search and filter on a phone, with structured data so roles can appear in Google\'s job search features.', 'CVs contain a lot of personal data, so application forms and storage need to be handled in line with UK GDPR and a clear privacy notice.'],
  'wedding-venue-website-design-uk': ['Couples shortlist venues on space, capacity, setting and rough cost, so make those easy to find before asking for an enquiry.', 'Whether a venue can host legal ceremonies depends on its approval with the local authority, so describe ceremony options accurately and hedge anything you are unsure of.', 'The main conversion goal is usually a date enquiry or show-round booking, and the form should ask for the details you actually need to reply well.'],
  'architect-website-design-uk': ['An architecture website is judged on its projects, so case studies need context, not just a gallery of beautiful photos.', 'Explain the services you offer and how working with you unfolds, because many clients have never commissioned an architect before.', 'Use the title architect only in line with ARB rules, credit photographers and collaborators, and keep image-heavy pages fast.'],
  'florist-website-design-uk': ['A florist website is mostly a delivery shop: make postcode coverage, delivery dates and cut-off times clear before checkout.', 'Design product pages for natural variation, with honest wording about seasonal substitutions and what the customer will receive.', 'Separate quick gift orders from wedding and event enquiries, which need a consultation-style route rather than a basket.'],
  'photographer-website-design-uk': ['A photography website should be organised around the services clients book, such as weddings or headshots, not just one long gallery.', 'Curate tightly, compress images properly and test on a phone, because slow, oversized galleries lose visitors.', 'Get consent before publishing people, be clear about pricing and what is included, and make the enquiry step easy.'],
  'physiotherapy-clinic-website-design-uk': ['Patients usually arrive with a specific problem, so pages organised around conditions and treatments help them decide whether to book.', 'Make booking simple and honest: show what an initial assessment involves, how long it takes and where prices can be found.', 'Describe treatments carefully, show registration details accurately and avoid claims about outcomes that you cannot support.'],
  'school-website-design-uk': ['A school website mostly serves current parents day to day, so term dates, letters, menus and contact details should be quick to find on a phone.', 'Many schools are required to publish certain information online; check the current Department for Education guidance for your type of school rather than relying on a generic checklist.', 'Choose a structure and platform that office staff can update confidently, and think about safeguarding before publishing any pupil images or names.'],
  'financial-adviser-website-design-uk': ['Prospective clients often want to understand who you help, how advice works and how you charge before they get in touch.', 'Website content is likely to count as a financial promotion or communication with clients, so involve your compliance function and check current FCA rules before publishing.', 'Regulatory status, charges and any claims about outcomes need careful, accurate wording, and this guide is not a substitute for compliance advice.'],
  'it-support-company-website-design-uk': ['Many people looking for IT support are not technical, so explaining services in terms of business outcomes and everyday problems usually works better than jargon.', 'Support hours, response targets and what plans include should be described accurately, and only in terms you actually commit to in contracts.', 'Security and certification claims carry real weight, so only show schemes and statuses you genuinely hold and describe their scope precisely.'],
  'letting-agent-website-design-uk': ['A letting agent\'s site usually serves two audiences with different needs, landlords choosing a manager and tenants looking for a home, so give each a clear path.', 'Fees, redress scheme membership and client money protection need to be displayed in line with the rules that apply in your part of the UK, so check current requirements.', 'Tools for existing tenants and landlords, such as maintenance reporting and portal logins, can reduce routine calls if they are easy to find.'],
  'manufacturer-website-design-uk': ['Industrial buyers and engineers often arrive with a specific requirement, so capability, material and tolerance information matters more than broad marketing copy.', 'Clear quote request routes, with a way to attach drawings, can make it easier for buyers to start a conversation.', 'Accreditations, certifications and compliance statements should be accurate and current, so only show what you actually hold.'],
  'restaurant-website-design-uk': ['Most restaurant visitors want a small number of things fast: the menu, the location, the opening hours and a way to book, so put those first.', 'Menus published as text pages, rather than only as downloadable files, are usually easier to read on a phone and easier for search engines to understand.', 'Allergen information, prices and booking terms need to be accurate and kept current, so check the rules that apply to your business and review them regularly.'],
  'dance-school-website-design-uk': ['Most dance school visitors want three things fast: which class suits their child or level, when it runs, and how to book a trial.', 'A timetable that is easy to update and readable on a phone matters more than any visual flourish.', 'Parents look for reassurance on safeguarding, teacher qualifications and policies, so make those easy to find without overclaiming.'],
  'engineering-consultancy-website-design-uk': ['Engineering consultancy buyers are often technical and cautious, so clarity and evidence matter more than slogans.', 'Project pages that explain the problem, your role and the outcome you can verify are the core of most consultancy sites.', 'The website also supports tenders and recruitment, so plan pages for procurement teams and candidates as well as clients.'],
  'event-planner-website-design-uk': ['An event planner website has to show taste and organisation at once: strong visuals backed by a clear process and practical detail.', 'Separate pages for each event type, such as corporate, private and charity events, help both visitors and search engines.', 'A well-designed enquiry form that asks for date, location, guest numbers and budget range saves time on every lead.'],
  'music-teacher-website-design-uk': ['A music teacher website should answer who you teach, what instruments and levels, where lessons happen and how to start.', 'Short, well-recorded audio or video of your teaching style often does more than long written biographies.', 'Clear lesson policies on cancellations, payment and safeguarding prevent misunderstandings before the first lesson.'],
  'sports-club-website-design-uk': ['A sports club website must be easy for volunteers to update, or it will quickly fall out of date.', 'New members need a clear route in: what the club offers, who it is for, when sessions run and how to join.', 'Junior sections need clear safeguarding information and careful handling of children\'s images and data.'],
  'bakery-cake-maker-website-design-uk': ['Custom cake customers usually want to see examples, understand rough pricing and know how far ahead to order.', 'Allergen information needs particular care for bakery products, so check current Food Standards Agency guidance for how you sell.', 'A bakery selling everyday bread and a cake maker taking bespoke orders often need quite different websites, so build for how you actually sell.'],
  'garden-centre-website-design-uk': ['Many garden centre visitors want practical details first: opening hours, location, parking and what is in stock or in season.', 'Selling live plants online raises particular questions about availability, delivery and plant health, so decide carefully what to sell online and how.', 'A garden centre site often serves several purposes at once, such as retail, a cafe, events and gift cards, so clear navigation matters.'],
  'logistics-courier-website-design-uk': ['Logistics buyers usually want to confirm quickly that you move their type of goods, cover their routes and can respond fast.', 'Separate pages for each service, such as same-day courier, pallet distribution or warehousing, tend to be easier to navigate and to rank than one long services page.', 'Licences, insurance and accreditations should be described accurately and only where you actually hold them, so check current requirements for your operation.'],
  'printing-company-website-design-uk': ['Print buyers usually want to know quickly whether you produce what they need, how much it costs and how soon it can arrive.', 'Clear artwork guidance and an easy upload route can reduce delays and back-and-forth on every order.', 'Whether to sell standard products online or quote for each job depends on your work mix, and many printers combine both.'],
  'saas-website-design-uk': ['Visitors to a software website usually need to understand what the product does, who it is for and how to try it within moments of arriving.', 'Pricing pages, trial or demo routes and product explanations tend to do more work on a SaaS site than on most other kinds of business website.', 'Security, data protection and accessibility claims should be accurate and specific, so check what you can genuinely support before publishing them.'],
  'aesthetics-clinic-website-design-uk': ['Prescription-only medicines such as botulinum toxin generally cannot be advertised to the public in the UK, which shapes how an aesthetics clinic website can describe some treatments.', 'Consultation-led booking, clear practitioner credentials and honest information about risks and recovery tend to build more trust than bold promises.', 'Rules in this area are detailed and change over time, so clinics should check current guidance from the ASA, CAP, MHRA and their own regulator, and take advice where needed.'],
  'chiropractor-osteopath-website-design-uk': ['Chiropractic and osteopathy websites need to explain treatment clearly while staying careful about health claims, which are subject to advertising rules and professional standards.', 'A clear guide to the first appointment, covering what happens, how long it takes and what it costs, can help nervous new patients take the step of booking.', 'Registration with the relevant statutory regulator is a meaningful trust signal, so it is worth showing accurately and linking to the official register where appropriate.'],
  'mortgage-broker-website-design-uk': ['A mortgage broker website is usually an enquiry tool first, so a clear, secure fact-find or enquiry form and simple next steps matter most.', 'Financial promotions rules and disclosure requirements apply to broker websites, so content should be checked against current FCA rules and, where relevant, your network\'s sign-off process.', 'Separate pages for first-time buyers, remortgages, buy-to-let and other situations help visitors find relevant information quickly.'],
  'tattoo-studio-website-design-uk': ['A tattoo studio website is mainly a portfolio and an enquiry tool, so artist pages and a clear booking request process usually matter more than anything else.', 'Spelling out deposits, cancellations, age requirements and aftercare in plain language can cut down repetitive messages and set expectations before anyone sits in the chair.', 'Licensing and registration for tattooing is handled locally in the UK, so studios should check the rules with their own council rather than relying on general guidance.'],
  'yoga-pilates-studio-website-design-uk': ['For most yoga and Pilates studios, the timetable and booking journey is the heart of the website, so it should be quick to use on a phone.', 'Beginners are often unsure which class to choose, so plain explanations of class types, levels and what to expect can make a real difference.', 'Class passes, memberships and intro offers should be explained clearly, with terms visible before anyone pays.'],
  'web-design-bristol': ['Bristol creative businesses need websites that show personality without sacrificing speed, clarity or a simple route to enquire.', 'Sustainable brands should keep environmental claims specific and evidenced, in line with CMA guidance, and can also build lighter, more efficient pages.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Bristol businesses remotely and has no office in the city.'],
  'web-design-cardiff': ['Bilingual Welsh and English websites need planning at the start: structure, language switching, translation workflow and SEO for both languages.', 'Firms that supply the public sector benefit from clear capability pages, policies and accessible design that buyers can check during evaluation.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Cardiff businesses remotely and has no office in Cardiff or Wales.'],
  'web-design-edinburgh': ['Edinburgh tourism and festival businesses need websites that cope with seasonal peaks, work well on phones and make booking direct easy.', 'Financial services firms need clarity, trust and careful wording, with regulatory information easy to find and claims kept accurate.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Edinburgh businesses remotely and has no office in the city.'],
  'web-design-nottingham': ['Nottingham retailers benefit from websites that connect online browsing with in-store visits, through accurate stock, opening hours and click and collect where it fits.', 'Businesses serving students should design for phones first and plan content around the academic year, from arrivals to exams and summer.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Nottingham businesses remotely and has no office in the city.'],
  'web-design-sheffield': ['Sheffield manufacturing and engineering websites need to answer technical buyers quickly: capabilities, materials, tolerances, certifications and how to request a quote.', 'Capability and sector pages built around real search terms tend to do more for B2B enquiries than a single long services page.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Sheffield businesses remotely, planning, designing and building sites without needing an office visit.'],
  'web-design-belfast': ['Belfast tech startups need sites that explain technical products simply, support hiring and stand up to scrutiny from customers and investors.', 'Northern Ireland businesses selling online may face different delivery, VAT and customs arrangements for GB, NI and EU customers, so check current rules and present them clearly.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Belfast businesses remotely, without an office in Northern Ireland.'],
  'web-design-leeds': ['Leeds professional services websites are judged on trust: clear expertise, visible regulation details, honest fee information and people a client can picture speaking to.', 'Regulated firms should check what their regulator expects on a website, such as price and complaints information, before a new site goes live.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Leeds businesses remotely, planning, writing and building sites over video calls and shared drafts.'],
  'web-design-leicester': ['Leicester textile and manufacturing firms often serve trade buyers and consumers at once, so the site structure should separate those journeys clearly.', 'Family businesses benefit from websites that capture the story and know-how of the firm while being simple enough for any family member or staff member to update.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Leicester businesses remotely, without needing site visits.'],
  'web-design-newcastle': ['Hospitality sites in Newcastle need to work on a phone in seconds: opening hours, menus, booking and directions should never be more than a tap away.', 'Startups usually benefit from a lean first site that tests a clear message, built on a platform that can grow, rather than a large site based on guesses.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Newcastle businesses remotely, from first plan to launch.'],
  'web-design-southampton': ['Maritime and marine service buyers include ship operators, yacht owners and contractors, often searching from abroad or at sea, so clarity and fast mobile pages matter.', 'Urgent services need an obvious emergency contact route, while project-based services need detail on capability, standards and coverage.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Southampton businesses remotely, from planning through to launch.'],
  'web-design-aberdeen': ['Aberdeen supply chain websites are often checked by procurement teams, so capabilities, certifications and contact routes should be easy to verify.', 'Firms moving into renewables and other sectors need sites that present transferable capability honestly rather than rebranding overnight.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Aberdeen businesses remotely, planning, writing and building sites over video calls and shared drafts.'],
  'web-design-brighton': ['Brighton independents often sell in a physical shop and online at once, so the website should keep stock, opening times and collection options in step with the shop.', 'Wellness practitioners need booking-led sites that explain sessions plainly, set expectations honestly and avoid health claims that cannot be backed up.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Brighton businesses remotely, planning, writing and building sites over video calls and shared drafts.'],
  'web-design-cambridge': ['A Cambridge startup website usually needs to change shape as the company moves from stealth to fundraising to commercial launch, so it should be built to evolve.', 'Life science companies should check what they can say about products in development, as rules on promoting medicines and medical devices are strict.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Cambridge businesses remotely, planning, writing and building sites over video calls and shared drafts.'],
  'web-design-oxford': ['Oxford research spinouts need websites that translate specialist work into plain language for investors, partners and future hires, without overstating what the research shows.', 'Education and visitor businesses often serve international audiences, so clear English, sensible currency and time-zone details and mobile-friendly booking matter.', 'Prism Works Studio works with Oxford businesses remotely, planning, writing and building sites over video calls and shared drafts.'],
  'web-design-york': ['York visitor businesses need sites that handle seasonal change, from opening hours to events, without the owner relying on a developer for every update.', 'Clear access information matters for historic buildings, where steps, narrow spaces and uneven floors are common and visitors want to plan ahead.', 'Prism Works Studio works with York businesses remotely, planning, writing and building sites over video calls and shared drafts.'],
  'web-design-coventry': ['Automotive supply chain buyers look for capability, quality systems and capacity, so make those easy to find.', 'Engineering firms moving into electrification or new sectors should restructure their sites around where they are heading, not only where they have been.', 'University spin-outs need websites that speak to investors, partners and early customers without overclaiming.'],
  'web-design-milton-keynes': ['Milton Keynes B2B sites usually serve several audiences at once, so plan separate routes for buyers, job seekers and partners.', 'Logistics and warehousing buyers want capability, coverage and compliance information quickly, without hunting through brochure copy.', 'Recruitment pages deserve proper design attention, because hiring for shift-based and specialist roles often runs through the website.'],
  'web-design-norwich': ['Norfolk food producers often sell to consumers, trade buyers and visitors at once; give each a separate route.', 'Agricultural businesses need sites that load well on rural connections and suit buyers who know exactly what they want.', 'Insurance and financial services sites should treat regulatory requirements as a design input, not an afterthought.'],
  'web-design-plymouth': ['Defence and marine suppliers need to show capability while respecting confidentiality; plan what can be published before writing.', 'Marine service and boat businesses benefit from clear service, location and seasonal information that works on a phone at the quayside.', 'Waterfront tourism sites should put sailings, sessions, tides or weather policies and bookings front and centre.'],
  'web-design-reading': ['Reading tech and IT sites often struggle to explain what they do in plain English; fix the message before the design.', 'Technical buyers and budget holders read differently, so give each the level of detail they need on the same page.', 'Demo, trial and contact routes should match how far along a buyer is, not push everyone straight to a sales call.'],
  'web-design-bath': ['A premium, calm design suits Bath\'s visitor market, but it must never slow down booking or buying.', 'Wellness businesses need to describe treatments carefully and avoid health claims they cannot support.', 'Independent shops can turn visitors into repeat online customers with a well-run ecommerce site.'],
  'web-design-derby': ['Rail and aerospace buyers often check a supplier\'s website during pre-qualification, so treat it as part of your tender evidence.', 'Long programme lifecycles mean obsolescence, spares and through-life support content can matter as much as new-build capability.', 'Document control discipline belongs on the website too: dated, versioned downloads and accurate approvals.'],
  'web-design-exeter': ['Professional firms in a regional city serve clients across a wide rural area, so service-area and remote-meeting information matters.', 'Rural customers may have slower or patchy connections; lightweight pages and simple forms help everyone.', 'Farm, estate and countryside businesses often run several income streams, which needs careful site structure.'],
  'web-design-hull': ['Logistics and port service firms win work when buyers can quickly see services, capacity, routes and how to get a quote.', 'Renewables suppliers should show relevant capability and safety credentials accurately, without implying project roles they did not have.', 'Food processors selling to trade need clear product, accreditation and specification information for buyers and technical teams.'],
  'web-design-swansea': ['Decide early how Welsh and English will work together on the site, because it shapes structure, navigation and search.', 'Coastal tourism and activity sites need live availability, clear conditions policies and pages that work on a phone outdoors.', 'Plan content around the seasons: peak bookings, shoulder-season offers and quieter-month local trade.'],
  'freelancer-vs-agency-website-uk': ['Neither a freelancer nor an agency is automatically better; the right choice depends on your project\'s scope, skills required and support needs.', 'Freelancers can offer a direct relationship, while agencies can bring a broader mix of skills and more capacity, but individual providers vary widely.', 'Whoever you choose, check relevant work, ownership arrangements, continuity plans and post-launch support.'],
  'how-long-to-build-a-website-uk': ['There is no single answer: scope, content readiness, platform, integrations and feedback speed all shape how long a website build takes.', 'Content and decisions on the client side are often what sets the pace, so preparing them early is one of the best ways to avoid delays.', 'Ask any web designer for a written schedule with stages, dependencies and a launch plan rather than a single headline date.'],
  'how-to-choose-a-web-designer-uk': ['Prepare a short brief before you approach anyone, so you can compare proposals on a like-for-like basis.', 'Judge designers on relevant work, clarity of process, who owns what at the end and what happens after launch, not on visuals alone.', 'Ask specific questions about scope, content, platform, SEO, ownership and support, and get the answers in writing.'],
  'website-ownership-and-handover': ['Paying for a website does not automatically mean you control every part of it, so agree ownership of domains, accounts, code and content in writing.', 'Keep key accounts such as the domain, hosting, platform and analytics in your business\'s name, with admin access you control.', 'A clear handover, with logins, documentation and backups, makes it far easier to change provider or bring work in-house later.'],
  'website-terms-and-privacy-policy-uk': ['Websites that collect personal data generally need a privacy notice, and online shops have extra information duties under consumer law.', 'Terms and conditions, privacy notices and cookie information do different jobs, so treat them as separate documents.', 'Use guidance from UK regulators as a starting point, keep documents accurate to how your site actually works, and take legal advice for your situation.'],
  'change-website-hosting-without-downtime': ['Set up and test the site on the new host before changing DNS, so visitors keep seeing the old site until the new one is ready.', 'Lower your DNS TTL in advance and keep the old hosting running until the change has fully spread.', 'Map every DNS record, especially email records, before you move, so email and other services keep working.'],
  'how-to-brief-a-shopify-developer': ['A good Shopify brief explains the business goal, the current store set-up and what done looks like, not just a list of features.', 'Share access, data and design files in an organised way, and say which apps, integrations and markets the store must support.', 'Written acceptance criteria and a clear change process help both sides agree when work is finished.'],
  'website-analytics-for-small-business': ['Start with what the website is for, define the actions that matter, then measure those before anything else.', 'Google Analytics shows what people do on your site; Google Search Console shows how you appear in search. Together they cover the essentials.', 'Look at trends over time and act on them; a short monthly review is more useful than a dashboard nobody opens.'],
  'website-backup-and-recovery-plan': ['A backup only counts if you can restore it, so test restores rather than assuming they work.', 'Back up files and database separately from your host, keep more than one copy and store at least one away from the live server.', 'Hosted platforms such as Shopify, Wix and Squarespace look after the platform, but your own content and data may still need exporting.'],
  'wordpress-plugin-audit': ['Audit plugins by asking of each one: is it needed, is it maintained, does it overlap with another, and what does it cost in speed and risk.', 'Always back up and test on a staging copy before deactivating or removing plugins on a live site.', 'Deactivated plugins should usually be deleted, and the audit repeated regularly rather than once.'],
  'google-merchant-center-setup-uk': ['Merchant Center is where Google gets your product data, both for free listings and for Shopping ads, so the quality of the feed matters before any money is spent.', 'Most disapprovals come from mismatches between the feed and the website, such as prices, stock status or missing policy pages.', 'Set up shipping, returns and business details carefully at the start, because they affect eligibility across every product.'],
  'how-to-add-a-blog-to-shopify': ['Shopify includes a built-in blog, so you can add one without extra apps or a separate website.', 'A shop blog earns its place by answering questions your customers search for and linking them to relevant products and collections.', 'Set titles, descriptions, URLs and image alt text for every post, and keep the blog easy to find in your navigation.'],
  'online-shop-shipping-rates-uk': ['Decide your delivery strategy first, then configure the platform; the settings are easy once you know what you want to charge.', 'Accurate product weights and sensible packaging assumptions are the foundation of any rate that is not a simple flat fee.', 'Test every zone and rate at checkout before launch, including awkward cases such as remote postcodes and very heavy baskets.'],
  'payment-gateways-uk-online-shop': ['A payment gateway is the part of your shop that securely takes card and wallet payments and passes the money on to you.', 'Compare gateways on total cost, payout timing, supported payment methods, checkout experience and how disputes are handled, not on headline rates alone.', 'Using a hosted or embedded gateway from a major provider keeps most card data off your own website, which reduces your security burden.'],
  'shopify-inventory-management': ['Turn on inventory tracking and give every variant a unique SKU before anything else; accurate stock starts with clean product data.', 'Decide deliberately whether each product can be sold when out of stock, rather than leaving the default in place.', 'Regular stock counts and recorded adjustments keep Shopify in line with what is actually on your shelves.'],
  'ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery': ['Fix the reasons people abandon first: surprise costs, forced accounts, slow pages and unclear delivery.', 'Reminder emails work best when they are helpful, brief and sent only where you have a lawful basis.', 'Treat abandoned baskets as feedback about your checkout, not only as a list of people to chase.'],
  'ecommerce-discount-code-strategy': ['Give every discount a clear purpose, such as a first order, a clearance or a loyalty reward.', 'Limit codes by audience, products, dates and usage so they cannot leak and run indefinitely.', 'Keep price and discount claims accurate, and check current UK pricing guidance before big sales.'],
  'website-breadcrumb-navigation': ['Breadcrumbs show visitors where they are and give a quick route back up the site structure.', 'They suit sites with depth, such as shops and large service sites, more than small flat sites.', 'Use clear labels, accessible markup and structured data that matches what visitors see.'],
  'website-call-to-action-buttons': ['A good call to action says what happens next in plain words, such as Book a call or Get a quote.', 'Give each page one main action and make it visually stronger than everything else on the page.', 'Place the button where the visitor has enough information to decide, not only at the very top.'],
  'website-redirects-when-relaunching': ['Map every important old URL to its closest new equivalent before launch, not after.', 'Use permanent redirects for moved pages and avoid chains, loops and mass redirects to the homepage.', 'Check redirects, Google Search Console and broken links in the days and weeks after going live.'],
  'shopify-apps-audit': ['List every installed app with its purpose, owner, permissions and whether anyone still uses it before deciding anything.', 'Uninstalling an app does not always remove the code it added to your theme, so check and clean up afterwards.', 'Test changes on a duplicate theme first and keep a record of what you removed and why.'],
  'shopify-collections-structure': ['Plan collections around how shoppers think about your range, not around how your stockroom or supplier list is organised.', 'Use automated collections with clear tag or field rules for anything that changes often, and manual collections for curated edits.', 'Treat each important collection as a landing page with a unique title, intro copy and description, then link to it from menus.'],
  'shopify-metafields-guide': ['Metafields store extra structured information, such as materials or care instructions, that standard Shopify fields do not cover.', 'Plan definitions and value types before entering data, so information stays consistent and can power filters.', 'Online Store themes can display metafields through dynamic sources in the theme editor, often without custom code.'],
  'wordpress-child-themes': ['A child theme holds your custom code separately, so updating the parent theme does not wipe out your changes.', 'You only need one if you are editing theme files or adding theme-level code; settings and content changes do not require it.', 'With block themes, many design changes live in the Site Editor, so check where a change belongs before creating a child theme.'],
  'wordpress-user-roles': ['Give each person the lowest WordPress role that lets them do their job, and keep Administrator accounts to a minimum.', 'Every person should have their own login so you can see who changed what and remove access cleanly.', 'Review user accounts regularly and remove anyone who no longer needs access, especially former staff and suppliers.'],
  'shopify-product-filters': ['Filters let shoppers narrow a collection by attributes such as size, colour, price, availability or material.', 'Shopify\'s Search and Discovery app controls which filters appear, and metafields allow filters based on custom product details.', 'Good filters depend on clean, consistent product data, so tidy your variants, tags and metafields first.'],
  'shopify-staff-accounts-and-permissions': ['Give every person their own Shopify login rather than sharing the store owner\'s account.', 'Grant only the permissions each person needs, and review access whenever roles change or people leave.', 'Agencies and developers should usually access your store through collaborator accounts, which you can approve and remove.'],
  'wordpress-block-editor-guide': ['The block editor builds every page from individual blocks, such as paragraphs, images, buttons and columns.', 'Patterns and synced patterns help editors build consistent layouts without starting from scratch each time.', 'A well-configured editor, with sensible styles and limited options, keeps a site consistent as more people edit it.'],
  'wordpress-custom-post-types': ['Custom post types let you store distinct kinds of content, such as projects, team members or case studies, separately from ordinary posts and pages.', 'They work best alongside custom taxonomies and custom fields, which give the content consistent structure.', 'Register custom post types in a plugin rather than a theme, so your content does not disappear if the design changes.'],
  'wordpress-multisite-guide': ['WordPress Multisite runs several websites from one WordPress installation, sharing core files, themes, plugins and users.', 'It suits organisations with many similar sites managed centrally, but adds complexity and shared risk.', 'Separate installations or a single site with well-structured sections are often simpler alternatives worth comparing first.'],
  'shopify-checkout-settings': ['Shopify\'s checkout settings control what customers are asked for, how accounts work and how marketing consent is collected.', 'Asking only for information you genuinely need keeps the checkout simple and supports good data protection practice.', 'Test every change by placing test orders on mobile and desktop before relying on it.'],
  'shopify-theme-updates': ['Theme updates can bring bug fixes, new features and compatibility improvements, but they do not apply to your live theme automatically.', 'Code edits made directly to a theme are the main reason updates become difficult, so keep a record of every customisation.', 'Always update a copy, test it thoroughly in preview and publish only when you are confident it works.'],
  'wordpress-comment-spam': ['WordPress includes discussion settings that can significantly reduce spam without any extra tools.', 'Many business sites do not need comments at all, and switching them off removes the problem entirely.', 'Where comments are useful, combine moderation, sensible settings and spam filtering, and review them regularly.'],
  'wordpress-database-cleanup': ['A WordPress database gathers revisions, spam, expired temporary data and leftovers from removed plugins over time.', 'Always take a full, tested backup and ideally work on a staging copy before deleting anything from the database.', 'Regular light housekeeping and sensible settings are safer than occasional aggressive clean-ups.'],
  'wordpress-media-library-organisation': ['Consistent file names, titles and alt text make media easier to find, more accessible and more useful for search.', 'Deleting media that looks unused can break pages, so check carefully and back up before removing anything.', 'Agreeing simple upload habits early prevents the media library becoming a cluttered archive.'],
  'shopify-draft-orders': ['Draft orders let you create an order in the Shopify admin on a customer\'s behalf, then send an invoice or mark it as paid.', 'They suit phone and email orders, custom pricing, trade customers and orders that need manual adjustments.', 'Check stock, taxes and shipping carefully, because draft orders give staff more freedom than the normal checkout.'],
  'shopify-gift-wrapping-and-order-notes': ['Shopify does not include a dedicated gift wrapping feature, but you can offer it as a product, a variant option or through cart attributes.', 'Cart notes and custom fields let customers leave gift messages and instructions, as long as your team actually reads them.', 'Whatever approach you choose, make the option clear, price it transparently and build it into your fulfilment process.'],
  'website-favicon-and-app-icons': ['A favicon is the small icon shown in browser tabs, bookmarks and search results, and it helps people recognise your site.', 'Prepare a simple, square version of your logo mark that still reads clearly at very small sizes.', 'WordPress and Shopify both let you upload a site icon without code, but check how it looks across devices afterwards.'],
  'wordpress-menus-guide': ['How you edit menus in WordPress depends on whether your site uses a block theme or a classic theme.', 'Menus should reflect how visitors think about your content, not your internal structure or every page you have.', 'Check menus on mobile and with a keyboard after every change, because dropdowns often behave differently there.'],
  'wordpress-revisions-and-autosave': ['WordPress saves revisions of posts and pages so you can compare changes and restore an earlier version.', 'Autosave is a separate safety net that protects unsaved work if your browser closes or your connection drops.', 'Revisions are not a backup: they only cover content, and only for posts and other types that support them.'],
  'shopify-local-pickup': ['Shopify\'s local pickup option lets customers order online and collect from a shop, studio or warehouse you choose.', 'Clear pickup instructions, accurate stock at each location and prompt ready-for-pickup emails are what make click and collect feel reliable.', 'A simple handover routine in store, including checking the order and marking it collected, avoids confusion on both sides.'],
  'shopify-pre-orders': ['Pre-orders let customers commit to a product before it is in stock, but only work well when expectations about dispatch are crystal clear.', 'Decide early whether to take full payment, a deposit or no payment upfront, because that choice shapes the setup on Shopify.', 'Keep pre-order products, stock levels and customer emails tidy so that orders can be fulfilled smoothly once stock lands.'],
  'website-maintenance-mode-page': ['A maintenance mode page tells visitors a site is temporarily unavailable and should explain what is happening and when to come back.', 'For temporary downtime, the page should return a 503 status code so that search engines understand it is not permanent.', 'Many updates can be tested on a staging site first, keeping time in maintenance mode as short as possible.'],
  'wordpress-synced-patterns': ['Synced patterns let you edit content in one place and have the change appear everywhere that pattern is used.', 'Unsynced patterns act as starting templates, so each copy can be edited independently without affecting the others.', 'A small, well-named library of patterns keeps pages consistent and makes it easier for your team to build new content.'],
  'wordpress-widgets-and-sidebars': ['Widgets are small content blocks shown in theme areas such as sidebars and footers, and how you manage them depends on whether your theme is classic or block-based.', 'Every widget should earn its place by helping visitors take a useful next step, not just filling space.', 'Sidebars can clutter mobile layouts and slow pages, so review them regularly and remove anything that does not serve a purpose.'],
  'shopify-order-fulfilment-workflow': ['Shopify separates payment status from fulfilment status, and understanding both is the foundation of a reliable dispatch routine.', 'A written, repeatable workflow for checking, picking, packing and marking orders as fulfilled reduces mistakes more than any single setting.', 'Tracking details, customer notifications and a clear returns process all belong to fulfilment, not just getting the parcel out of the door.'],
  'shopify-product-tags': ['Shopify product tags are simple labels, and their value comes from using them consistently across the whole catalogue.', 'Tags work well for internal organisation and automated collection rules, while metafields are often better for structured product information.', 'A short written tagging convention and an occasional tidy-up stop the tag list from becoming a source of errors.'],
  'website-print-stylesheets': ['A print stylesheet tells the browser how a page should look on paper or as a saved PDF, separately from how it looks on screen.', 'Good printed pages hide navigation, banners and buttons, keep the main content readable, and show the information people need offline.', 'Print styles are easy to forget during a build, so test key pages with the browser print preview as part of routine checks.'],
  'wordpress-permalink-settings': ['Permalinks control the web address of every post and page, so the structure is best decided early and changed rarely.', 'A simple, readable structure based on the post name suits many small business sites, but the right choice depends on how the content is organised.', 'Changing permalinks on a live site changes URLs, so plan redirects and testing before you press save.'],
  'wordpress-site-health-screen': ['Site Health is a built-in WordPress check that flags configuration, security and performance issues in plain language.', 'Critical issues deserve prompt attention, while recommended improvements can often be planned into routine maintenance.', 'Many fixes involve hosting or server settings, so check with your host and test on staging before changing anything significant.'],
  'shopify-customer-accounts': ['Shopify offers two account types: newer customer accounts that sign in with a one-time code, and classic accounts that use a password.', 'For most stores, keep accounts optional at checkout so nobody is forced to sign up before paying.', 'Check how your theme, apps and any customer-only content behave before switching account types, and test on a copy first.'],
  'shopify-navigation-menus': ['Shopify menus are built in Content, then Menus, and your theme decides where each menu appears.', 'Base the main menu on how customers shop, usually by collection, and keep labels short and familiar.', 'Check menus on mobile and with a keyboard, and review them whenever you add or retire collections.'],
  'shopify-url-redirects': ['Add a redirect whenever a product, collection, page or blog post address changes or is removed, so visitors and search engines reach the right place.', 'Point each old address straight to its closest equivalent, not to the homepage, and avoid chains of redirects.', 'Shopify redirects only work for addresses that no longer exist, so a live page at the old address will block them.'],
  'wordpress-reading-and-discussion-settings': ['Reading settings decide what your homepage shows, where your blog lives and whether search engines are discouraged from indexing the site.', 'Always check the search engine visibility box is unticked on a live site, especially after launching from a staging copy.', 'Discussion settings control comments, moderation and notifications, so set them to match how much time you can give to replies.'],
  'wordpress-scheduled-posts': ['Set the WordPress timezone to a city such as London, not a fixed UTC offset, so scheduled times follow British Summer Time changes.', 'WordPress publishes scheduled posts through its own task runner, which only fires when the site gets a visit or a server task triggers it.', 'If schedules are missed, check the timezone, caching, maintenance mode and whether your host runs a real server task.'],
  'shopify-customer-segments': ['Customer segments group shoppers by what they have bought, how they behave and what they have agreed to receive.', 'A handful of clear, purposeful segments is more useful than dozens nobody looks at.', 'Only market to customers who have given the right consent, and check current UK guidance on direct marketing rules.'],
  'shopify-shipping-profiles': ['Shipping profiles let you charge different rates for groups of products that cost different amounts to send.', 'Start with the general profile and only add custom profiles when a product genuinely needs different handling.', 'Test real baskets at checkout after every change, especially mixed baskets that combine products from different profiles.'],
  'wordpress-categories-and-tags': ['Categories are broad sections of your blog; tags describe more specific details within posts.', 'Plan a small set of categories in advance and use tags sparingly and consistently.', 'Every category and tag creates an archive page, so avoid creating many with only one or two posts.'],
  'wordpress-image-sizes-and-thumbnails': ['WordPress automatically creates several resized copies of each image you upload, and your theme may add more.', 'Uploading sensibly sized images and setting featured image dimensions consistently keeps pages sharp and fast.', 'When you change image settings, existing images are not resized automatically, so plan any regeneration carefully.'],
  'wordpress-site-editor-templates': ['Templates control the layout of whole types of page, while template parts are reusable sections such as headers and footers.', 'Patterns are for reusable content inside pages; templates and template parts are for site-wide structure.', 'Edit templates carefully, keep a record of changes and know how to reset a template to the theme default.'],
  'shopify-product-variants': ['Variants are versions of one product, such as sizes or colours, that share a single product page.', 'Deciding early whether something is a variant or a separate product saves a lot of rework later.', 'Each variant can carry its own price, SKU, stock level and image, so tidy data matters from day one.'],
  'shopify-store-policies': ['Shopify has a dedicated policies area that links your key policies into checkout and the store footer.', 'Templates are a starting point only; policies should reflect how your business actually operates.', 'UK consumer and data protection rules may apply, so take professional advice on the wording.'],
  'website-dark-mode-design': ['Dark mode is optional; it suits some sites and audiences more than others.', 'Good dark themes use dark greys and adjusted colours rather than simply inverting the light design.', 'Logos, images, forms and contrast all need checking in both modes before launch.'],
  'wordpress-automatic-updates': ['WordPress can update core, plugins and themes automatically, and each can be controlled separately.', 'Automatic updates close security gaps quickly but can occasionally break a site without warning.', 'Backups, monitoring and a staging site make any update approach far safer.'],
  'wordpress-site-editor-styles': ['Global styles let you set fonts, colours and spacing once for the whole site in a block theme.', 'A small, deliberate palette and type scale keeps editors on brand and pages consistent.', 'Style changes made in the editor are stored in the database, so document and back them up.'],
  'shopify-order-editing-and-refunds': ['Order editing lets you change items and quantities after checkout while keeping one clean order record.', 'Refunds should be issued against the original order so stock, reporting and customer emails stay accurate.', 'A short written process for edits, refunds and restocking prevents staff from handling the same situation in different ways.'],
  'shopify-theme-sections-and-blocks': ['Sections are the building units of a Shopify page, and blocks are the smaller pieces of content inside them.', 'Most modern themes let you add, reorder and hide sections on most templates using the theme editor without code.', 'Agreeing a small set of section patterns keeps pages consistent and makes the store easier to maintain.'],
  'website-pagination-vs-load-more': ['Pagination, load more and infinite scroll each suit different kinds of browsing, so match the pattern to what visitors are doing.', 'Whichever you choose, every item should be reachable through crawlable links so search engines can find it.', 'Keep the visitor\'s place when they return from an item, as losing it is one of the most frustrating browsing experiences.'],
  'website-sticky-header-design': ['A sticky header keeps key navigation and actions within reach as visitors scroll, which suits longer pages and online stores.', 'The best sticky headers are slim, uncluttered and leave plenty of the screen for content, especially on mobile.', 'Test sticky behaviour with keyboard users, zoomed text and anchor links, as these are where problems usually appear.'],
  'wordpress-search-results-page': ['The default WordPress search works, but its results page often needs better layout, context and a helpful empty state.', 'Decide which content types should appear in results and exclude pages that only add noise.', 'Looking at what visitors search for reveals gaps in your navigation and content.'],
  'shopify-sales-channels-overview': ['A sales channel is any place your Shopify products can be sold, all managed from one admin.', 'Products, stock and orders are shared across channels, so accurate product data matters everywhere.', 'Add channels gradually and only when you can support them with good listings and customer service.'],
  'shopify-search-and-discovery-settings': ['Shopify\'s built-in search relies heavily on the quality of your product titles, types, tags and descriptions.', 'Synonyms, filters and product boosts help shoppers find products using their own words.', 'Reviewing what people search for, and what returns nothing, shows where to improve next.'],
  'website-about-page-design': ['An about page should explain who you help and how, not only your history.', 'Specific, honest detail builds more trust than vague claims or buzzwords.', 'Every about page should end with a clear next step for interested visitors.'],
  'website-contact-page-design': ['A good contact page offers clear options and tells people what will happen after they get in touch.', 'Short, accessible forms that ask only for what you need make enquiries easier to send.', 'Contact details should be easy to find from every page, not hidden on one page alone.'],
  'wordpress-trash-and-restoring-content': ['Deleted posts and pages go to the trash first, where they can usually be restored with one click.', 'Items in the trash are removed permanently after a set period, so restore anything important promptly.', 'Regular backups and sensible user permissions are the real safety net for lost content.'],
  'shopify-inventory-transfers': ['Inventory transfers record stock moving between your Shopify locations so each location shows what it really holds.', 'Create the transfer when stock leaves, then receive it carefully at the destination, noting any shortfalls or damage.', 'Clear location names, regular counts and one person responsible for transfers keep the numbers trustworthy.'],
  'shopify-product-media-guide': ['Product media does the job a customer\'s hands would do in a shop, so plan it around the questions buyers ask.', 'Order media deliberately, link images to variants and write useful alt text for every file.', 'Video and 3D models can help with some products but add weight, so use them where they genuinely explain something.'],
  'website-form-error-messages': ['A good error message says what went wrong, where it happened and how to fix it, in plain language.', 'Show errors next to the field, keep what people typed, and never rely on colour alone.', 'Preventing errors with clear labels, examples and flexible input is better than catching them afterwards.'],
  'website-tables-on-mobile': ['Tables suit genuinely tabular information, but wide tables need a deliberate plan for small screens.', 'Common approaches include horizontal scrolling, stacked cards, hiding less important columns and splitting large tables.', 'Use proper table markup with headers so screen readers can make sense of the data.'],
  'wordpress-font-loading': ['Every font family, weight and style is a separate file the browser must download, so fewer is usually better.', 'Hosting fonts on your own site and using the site editor\'s font tools gives you more control over speed and privacy.', 'Sensible fallback fonts and font display settings stop text from vanishing or jumping while fonts load.'],
  'shopify-product-csv-import': ['Always export a fresh CSV backup before importing anything, so you can compare or roll back by hand.', 'The product handle is what Shopify uses to match rows to existing products, so never change it casually.', 'Test every import with a small file first, then check products, variants, images and prices in the admin.'],
  'website-accordions-and-tabs': ['Accordions and tabs can make long or varied content easier to scan, but they also hide it, so never tuck away information most visitors need.', 'Accordions tend to suit stacked questions and small screens, while tabs suit a small number of parallel, short-labelled views.', 'Clear labels, keyboard support and a sensible default state matter more than animation or visual polish.'],
  'website-image-alt-text-guide': ['Alt text describes the purpose and meaningful content of an image for people who cannot see it.', 'Good descriptions depend on context, so the same photo may need different wording on different pages.', 'Decorative images should usually have empty alt text, while logos, buttons and linked images need text that explains their function.'],
  'wordpress-front-page-and-posts-page': ['WordPress can show either your latest posts or a chosen static page as the homepage, and that choice lives under Settings then Reading.', 'A business site usually needs two published pages assigned here: one for the homepage and an empty one for the blog listing.', 'If the wrong design appears after the switch, check which template your theme uses for the homepage and for the posts listing.'],
  'wordpress-import-and-export-tools': ['The built-in export creates a file containing content such as posts, pages, comments, categories and tags, not a complete copy of your site.', 'Settings, themes, plugins and many customisations are not carried across, so an export is not a substitute for a backup.', 'Test every import on a staging site first, and check media, authors, links and layout before relying on the result.'],
  'shopify-connect-custom-domain': ['You can connect a domain you already own to Shopify and leave it with your current registrar, so a transfer is optional.', 'Only the web records need to change. Leave your MX and other email records alone and your mailboxes should carry on working.', 'Choose one primary domain, redirect the others to it, and check the secure certificate and every address variation after the change.'],
  'shopify-reports-and-analytics': ['Shopify analytics is the place to start for sales, orders and products because the figures come from your store\'s own records.', 'A metric on its own says little. Compare it with a sensible earlier period and look at what sits behind any change.', 'A short regular routine with a few agreed questions is more useful than checking every report whenever you feel worried.'],
  'shopify-vat-tax-settings-uk': ['Shopify calculates tax from the settings you give it, but deciding whether and how VAT applies to your business remains your responsibility.', 'UK shoppers generally expect to see prices including VAT, so decide this setting before you enter or import your catalogue.', 'Check non-standard products, shipping, discounts and invoices with a test order, then confirm the set-up with your accountant.'],
  'website-content-before-build': ['Website content delays are easier to avoid when one person owns the content and each page has a named supplier and a due date.', 'Start with a page list and a short brief for each page, so that you gather only what the site actually needs.', 'Check you have permission to use every image, logo and quote, and give your builder final wording rather than rough notes.'],
  'brand-strategy-vs-marketing-strategy': ['Brand strategy defines who you are, who you are for and why you should be chosen. Marketing strategy decides how you reach people and win their business.', 'The two depend on each other: brand gives marketing a consistent message, and marketing puts that message in front of the right people.', 'Which needs attention first depends on your situation, and a small business can often do a light version of both rather than a large exercise.'],
  'conversion-rate-optimisation-audit': ['A conversion rate optimisation audit should check that your data can be trusted before it draws any conclusions from that data.', 'A useful audit looks at whole journeys as well as single pages, including forms, checkout, trust signals, speed and mobile use.', 'The output should be a prioritised list of evidence-backed changes and test ideas, not a general list of design opinions.'],
  'google-ad-grants-uk-charities': ['Google Ad Grants offers eligible charities free search advertising, but eligibility and account rules can change, so always check Google\'s current terms.', 'A grant account needs active management, because it must meet Google\'s programme requirements and works best with clear goals and useful landing pages.', 'A standard paid Google Ads account can sit alongside a grant where a charity needs more flexibility, but that spend needs a clear purpose.'],
  'google-shopping-feed-campaign-management': ['Good Google Shopping management starts with the product feed, because Shopping ads are built from your product data rather than from keywords you write.', 'Campaign structure should reflect commercial differences such as margin, stock and seasonality, not simply copy the layout of your online shop.', 'Ongoing work means regular feed and account checks, search term reviews and reporting tied to profit, not one-off set-up.'],
  'how-to-choose-marketing-agency-school-college': ['Start with your enrolment or recruitment goal and your internal capacity, then look for an agency whose skills fit that brief.', 'Ask how an agency handles safeguarding, pupil images and personal data, since these matter more in education than in most sectors.', 'Check who will do the work, how results are reported and what you own if you part ways, and be wary of guaranteed outcomes.'],
  'ecommerce-photography-brief': ['A good photography brief turns what shoppers need to know about a product into a clear shot list, so images answer questions rather than simply look attractive.', 'Agree the practical details in writing before the shoot, including samples, style references, crops, file formats, naming, retouching limits and how images may be used.', 'A brief is just as useful when you shoot in-house, because it keeps images consistent as your range grows and different people take the photographs.'],
  'multi-location-seo-audit': ['A multi-location SEO audit checks each branch and the system around it, comparing profiles, location pages, business details, links, reviews and reporting.', 'Use one simple spreadsheet with a row for every branch, because it reveals patterns that are easy to miss when you review locations one at a time.', 'Tackle problems that affect many branches or could send customers to the wrong place first, such as wrong details, duplicate profiles or weak page templates.'],
  'recruitment-agency-employer-marketing': ['Employer-focused marketing works best when an agency can clearly say who it recruits for, which roles it fills and why a hiring manager should choose it.', 'Useful sector pages, honest hiring content and a consistent presence on LinkedIn give employers evidence of knowledge before they make contact.', 'Track employer enquiries separately from candidate activity, because job applications can make marketing look busy while saying little about new client work.'],
  'website-support-plan-what-to-include': ['A useful support plan names who does what: updates, backups, security checks, fixes and reporting, along with how requests are handled and what sits outside the plan.', 'Without a plan, problems tend to build quietly through missed updates, untested backups and broken forms, and they are often found only when something has already gone wrong.', 'Read the terms before you compare prices, because two plans with the same name can cover very different amounts of work and responsibility.'],
  'ebay-seo-uk': ['eBay SEO means making listings easy for buyers and for eBay search to match, using accurate titles, complete item specifics and clear product information.', 'Findability is only part of the job, because photos, price, delivery, returns and your seller record can all affect whether a buyer chooses you.', 'Work through your best sellers first, change one thing at a time where possible, and judge results on sales and profit rather than views alone.'],
  'international-seo-agency-uk': ['International SEO helps the right version of your site reach people in each target country and language, which takes more than translating existing pages.', 'Decisions on markets, URL structure, hreflang and localisation should come before content production, because they are harder and riskier to change later.', 'A good agency will challenge whether a market is ready, and will plan for the local operations, content and upkeep that each new version of the site needs.'],
  'linkedin-ads-agency-uk': ['A LinkedIn Ads agency plans targeting, creative, lead capture and measurement so your campaigns reach the right decision-makers and produce useful sales conversations.', 'The channel tends to suit B2B businesses with a clearly defined audience and customers valuable enough to justify the cost of reaching them.', 'Choose a provider that reports on qualified leads and pipeline, and that ties campaign work to your sales process rather than clicks and impressions.'],
  'microsoft-ads-management-uk': ['Microsoft Ads can add extra search demand alongside Google Ads, but its value depends on whether your audience, product and tracking suit a separate test.', 'An imported Google Ads campaign is a useful starting point rather than a finished account, because settings, audiences, search terms and bids all need checking.', 'Judge the channel on qualified enquiries or profitable sales, measured separately, rather than on cheaper clicks alone.'],
  'technical-seo-agency-uk': ['A technical SEO agency finds and helps fix the problems that stop search engines crawling, understanding and indexing your important pages.', 'A useful audit ranks issues by business impact and says who needs to do what, rather than handing you a long list of automated warnings.', 'Check whether a provider will implement fixes or only recommend them, because findings that never reach your live site will not help.'],
  'ai-seo-agency-uk': ['An AI SEO agency uses artificial intelligence to speed up research, analysis and content planning, while people stay responsible for strategy, accuracy and final decisions.', 'AI SEO is about how the work gets done, while GEO is about being visible and cited in AI-generated answers, so check which of the two a provider is offering.', 'Choose a provider by asking how it checks AI output, how it protects your data and how it links the work to enquiries or sales rather than volume.'],
  'bespoke-website-design-agency-uk': ['A bespoke website design agency creates a site around your brand, customers and goals rather than adapting a ready-made template.', 'Custom design tends to be worth it when your brand, your content or your customer journey cannot be served well by an off-the-shelf layout.', 'Ask what bespoke actually means in each proposal, because the term is used loosely and may refer to design, code or both.'],
  'bq-marketplace-seo-uk': ['B&Q Marketplace listings are more likely to be found when titles, categories and product attributes are complete, accurate and match how customers search.', 'Home and garden buyers often need practical detail such as size, material, compatibility and what is included, so good listings answer those questions before they are asked.', 'Platform rules and requirements can change, so always check current B&Q seller guidance and work from accurate product data.'],
  'shopify-store-management-uk': ['Shopify store management is ongoing help with running a store, such as product updates, theme changes, app reviews, promotions and reporting.', 'Keep decisions that depend on your brand and customers close to home, and consider outsourcing technical or repetitive work your team has no time for.', 'Before you sign, agree the scope, response times, staff access, ownership and how out-of-scope work will be charged.'],
  'website-redesign-agency-uk': ['A website redesign agency rebuilds how your site looks and works, and a good one also protects the search visibility and content you have already earned.', 'Start by naming the business problem, because some problems can be solved with targeted fixes instead of a full redesign.', 'Compare providers on how they handle migration, content, ownership and post-launch support, as well as on the look of their design work.'],
  'car-dealership-marketing-uk': ['Independent dealers benefit from a strong own website alongside portals, so trust, stock and enquiries are not all rented.', 'Fast, detailed vehicle pages with real photos, clear specs and simple enquiry options are the core of a dealer website.', 'Local SEO and tightly targeted search and remarketing ads usually outperform broad brand campaigns for smaller dealers.'],
  'coworking-space-marketing-uk': ['Most coworking members choose a space after a visit, so every page and ad should lead to booking a tour or a free day.', 'Clear membership options and starting prices help freelancers, small teams and hybrid workers self-select quickly.', 'Local SEO, meeting room searches and a steady flow of community content usually outperform broad brand advertising.'],
  'flooring-company-website-design-uk': ['A flooring website should lead visitors to one main action, usually booking a free or paid home measure or a showroom visit.', 'Photos of real fitted rooms, organised by product and room type, sell better than manufacturer imagery alone.', 'Local service area pages and product guides help carpet and flooring firms rank for the searches customers actually use.'],
  'google-ads-conversion-tracking-setup': ['Decide which actions really matter, such as calls, forms or purchases, before touching any settings.', 'Set up tracking with a Google tag, Tag Manager or a GA4 import, then test every conversion.', 'Respect UK cookie consent rules and keep primary conversions focused so bidding learns from real value.'],
  'google-ads-negative-keywords-guide': ['Negative keywords block searches you do not want to pay for, such as jobs, free or DIY queries.', 'Find them in the search terms report and add them at the right level: campaign, ad group or shared list.', 'Review search terms regularly, because new irrelevant queries appear as campaigns run.'],
  'google-business-profile-posts-guide': ['Posts add fresh, useful information to your profile where local customers already look.', 'Use updates, offers and events with a clear photo and a single call to action.', 'A short, regular routine beats bursts of activity followed by months of silence.'],
  'google-search-console-setup-uk': ['Add a Domain property where you can, verify through your DNS, then submit your sitemap.', 'The Performance, Pages and Experience reports show what Google sees and where to act.', 'Give access to people who need it, and remove access when a supplier relationship ends.'],
  'how-to-respond-to-google-reviews-uk': ['Reply to every review, positive or negative, within a few working days and in a calm, specific voice.', 'Never share customer details or argue in public; move complaints to a private channel.', 'Flag reviews that break Google policy, but do not rely on removal as your main strategy.'],
  'self-storage-marketing-uk': ['Most storage enquiries start with a local search, so Google Business Profile and location pages matter more than anything else.', 'A clear unit size guide and simple online quote or reservation remove the biggest reasons people phone a competitor instead.', 'Paid search works for storage when it is tightly local, tied to life events and measured on reservations rather than clicks.'],
  'soft-play-centre-marketing-uk': ['Parents decide quickly on a phone, so session times, prices, age ranges and online booking must be obvious on every page.', 'Birthday parties are often the most valuable bookings, so give them their own page with packages and an easy enquiry route.', 'Local search, school holiday planning and social ads aimed at nearby parents usually beat broad awareness campaigns.'],
  'boarding-kennel-cattery-marketing-uk': ['Owners are choosing who looks after a family member, so transparency about facilities, routines and licensing outweighs clever slogans.', 'Local search, a complete Google Business Profile and steady reviews drive most enquiries for boarding kennels and catteries.', 'Peak holiday periods book up early, so marketing effort should go into the months before summer, Easter and Christmas.'],
  'car-valeting-detailing-marketing-uk': ['Customers buy valeting and detailing by sight, so honest before-and-after photos and clear service descriptions do much of the selling.', 'Local search and Google Business Profile drive most enquiries, whether you run a unit or a mobile service.', 'Clear packages, simple online booking and steady reviews turn one-off jobs into repeat maintenance customers.'],
  'email-list-building-uk': ['Build an email list by offering a clear reason to subscribe, placing simple sign-up forms where interested visitors already are, and following up with a welcome email.', 'In the UK, PECR and UK GDPR shape who you can email and how you record consent, so never buy lists and keep clear records.', 'A smaller list of engaged subscribers is worth more than a large list of people who never open, so clean your list regularly.'],
  'escape-room-marketing-uk': ['Most escape room bookings start with a local search, so Google Business Profile, room pages and reviews do the heavy lifting.', 'Every room needs its own page with difficulty, group size, duration and accessibility details, linked straight to live availability.', 'Paid search and social work best when aimed at specific audiences and quiet slots, such as weekday corporate sessions or birthday parties.'],
  'google-ads-responsive-search-ads': ['Responsive search ads let you supply multiple headlines and descriptions, and Google mixes them to suit each search, so every line must make sense on its own.', 'Plan headlines by job (keyword match, offer, proof, location, call to action) rather than writing variations of the same sentence.', 'Use pinning sparingly, treat ad strength as a guide not a goal, and judge ads on conversions from accurate tracking.'],
  'holiday-park-marketing-uk': ['Direct bookings depend on a fast website, clear accommodation pages and a booking journey that feels as easy as the big listing platforms.', 'Destination content about the surrounding area helps a park appear when people are still deciding where to holiday.', 'Seasonal timing matters: most of the marketing effort should land in the planning months before the peak season.'],
  'local-citations-uk': ['Local citations are mentions of your business name, address and phone number on other websites, and consistent details help search engines and customers trust your listing.', 'Start with your Google Business Profile and a short list of major and relevant UK directories before chasing volume.', 'Cleaning up old or wrong listings, such as a previous address or phone number, is often more valuable than creating new ones.'],
  'meta-pixel-setup-guide': ['The Meta Pixel records actions people take on your website after seeing Facebook or Instagram ads, so Meta can report results and optimise delivery.', 'Track a small number of events that match real business outcomes, such as leads or purchases, and test each one before spending money on ads.', 'Under UK GDPR and PECR, advertising tracking generally needs consent, so connect the pixel to your cookie banner and consider the Conversions API for resilience.'],
  'riding-school-equestrian-centre-marketing-uk': ['Parents and adult beginners need reassurance on safety, ability levels and what to wear, so clear lesson pages matter more than slogans.', 'Local search and Google Business Profile bring in most new riders, supported by honest reviews and real photos.', 'Holiday camps, pony days and livery each need their own pages and seasonal timing in your marketing calendar.'],
  'utm-tracking-links-guide': ['UTM tracking links add short labels to a web address so analytics tools can tell you which email, post, QR code or ad sent each visitor.', 'A simple written naming convention, used consistently in lower case, matters more than any tool and keeps your GA4 reports readable.', 'Never put personal data in UTM values, never tag internal links on your own site, and check that auto-tagged ad platforms are not being overwritten.'],
  'dog-trainer-marketing-uk': ['Most dog training clients search locally for a specific problem or stage, such as puppy classes or recall, so your pages should match those needs.', 'Owners want to understand your approach before they book, so explain your methods, experience and what a session looks like in plain language.', 'A simple website with online booking, a strong Google Business Profile and steady reviews usually does more than heavy advertising.'],
  'dry-cleaner-marketing-uk': ['Most dry cleaning customers choose from the map results, so a complete Google Business Profile and steady reviews are the foundation of your marketing.', 'A simple website with clear services, prices or price guidance, turnaround times and collection options answers the questions people ask before visiting.', 'Specialist services such as wedding dress cleaning, alterations and business accounts deserve their own pages, because they attract higher-value customers.'],
  'google-ads-location-targeting-guide': ['Set locations to match the area you can genuinely serve, using towns, postcode areas or a radius around your premises.', 'Check the presence setting so ads reach people in your area, not just people who show interest in it.', 'Use location reports to adjust bids or exclude areas once real data comes in.'],
  'looker-studio-dashboard-guide': ['Decide the handful of questions the dashboard must answer before connecting any data.', 'Connect GA4, Search Console and Google Ads through Google connectors, then build one page per audience or channel.', 'Keep it small: a few clear charts, sensible date comparisons and notes beat dozens of tables nobody reads.'],
  'marquee-hire-marketing-uk': ['Marquee hire is a considered, high-value purchase, so your website must answer sizing, layout, site and timing questions before people will enquire.', 'Local SEO should reflect the area you actually cover, with service area pages that are genuinely useful rather than copied town lists.', 'Fast, organised follow-up on enquiries and site visits often matters as much as the marketing that produced the enquiry.'],
  'meta-lookalike-audiences-guide': ['A lookalike is only as good as its source: use buyers or qualified leads rather than every website visitor.', 'Customer lists must be collected and uploaded in line with UK GDPR and your privacy notice.', 'Test lookalikes against broad targeting, because Meta often finds similar people on its own.'],
  'title-tags-and-meta-descriptions-guide': ['Write a unique title tag for every page that leads with the main search phrase and stays short enough to display in full.', 'Use the meta description to answer the query and give a reason to click, even though Google may rewrite it.', 'Check Search Console for pages with impressions but few clicks, and rewrite those titles first.'],
  'trampoline-park-marketing-uk': ['Most trampoline park bookings start with a parent searching locally, so Google Business Profile, reviews and a fast mobile booking journey matter most.', 'Parties, toddler sessions, school groups and fitness classes each need their own page and their own marketing, because they fill different times of the week.', 'Paid social and search work best when aimed at specific sessions and audiences, with clear offer terms and conversion tracking on completed bookings.'],
  'vineyard-winery-marketing-uk': ['A UK vineyard website has three jobs at once: selling bottles online, booking tours and tastings, and taking enquiries for events.', 'Local search and a strong Google Business Profile bring in day visitors, while content about your site, grapes and wines builds trust with buyers further away.', 'Email and wine clubs turn a single cellar door visit into repeat orders, provided marketing consent is captured properly and age checks are in place.'],
  'xml-sitemap-guide': ['An XML sitemap lists the important, indexable pages on your site so search engines can find them more easily.', 'Most platforms create one automatically; your job is to check it lists the right pages and nothing broken.', 'Submit it in Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools, then watch the reports for errors.'],
  'bowling-alley-marketing-uk': ['Busy weekends often look after themselves, so the real marketing job is filling weekday and daytime lanes with targeted offers and groups.', 'Online lane booking with clear prices, game lengths and food options turns casual searches into confirmed visits.', 'Parties, corporate socials, leagues and food and drink packages each need their own pages and campaigns to bring in higher-value bookings.'],
  'ga4-explorations-guide': ['Explorations are GA4\'s custom analysis area, useful when the standard reports cannot answer a specific question about visitors, pages or conversions.', 'Free form, funnel and path explorations cover most small business needs: comparing channels, finding where people drop out, and seeing what visitors do next.', 'Start each exploration from a written question, check your date range and key events first, and remember explorations are personal workspaces rather than shared dashboards.'],
  'go-karting-track-marketing-uk': ['Most karting bookings start with a local search or a group organiser comparing options, so your listing, reviews and package pages need to answer questions fast.', 'A booking journey that shows live availability, prices and age or height rules turns interest into confirmed sessions without a phone call.', 'Separate pages and campaigns for parties, stag and hen groups, corporate events and leagues let you target each audience with the right message.'],
  'google-ads-assets-guide': ['Assets, once called extensions, add extra links, short selling points, a phone number, location and more to search ads, making them larger and more useful.', 'Most UK small businesses should start with sitelinks, callouts, structured snippets and a call or location asset, all written to match the landing pages behind them.', 'Google decides when assets show, so add a good range, keep them accurate, and review the asset performance figures rather than expecting every one to appear every time.'],
  'how-to-write-an-email-newsletter': ['A good small business newsletter has one main message, a specific subject line, short scannable sections and a single clear call to action.', 'Consistency matters more than length: a short, useful email sent on a regular schedule builds more trust than an occasional long one.', 'Send only to people who have agreed to hear from you, make unsubscribing easy, test on mobile, and track clicks and enquiries rather than opens alone.'],
  'internal-linking-guide-small-business': ['Internal links tell search engines which pages matter most and help visitors move from general information to the page where they can buy or enquire.', 'Plan links around a few priority money pages, link to them from relevant blog posts and service pages, and use descriptive anchor text rather than click here.', 'Review links whenever you publish, redesign or remove pages, and fix orphan pages and broken links so no useful page is left unreachable.'],
  'pottery-painting-studio-marketing-uk': ['Customers usually find a paint-your-own studio through a local search or social post, so your listing, photos and reviews need to show the experience clearly.', 'Online table booking, clear studio fees and pottery prices, and firing and collection times answer the questions that stop people visiting.', 'Parties, workshops, hen groups, corporate sessions and gift vouchers each deserve their own page because they bring higher-value bookings.'],
  'robots-txt-guide-uk': ['Robots.txt is a short public text file that asks crawlers not to visit certain paths; it does not hide pages from Google search results on its own.', 'The most common small business problem is a leftover rule from a staging site that blocks the whole website, so check the file after every launch or migration.', 'Edit robots.txt through your platform\'s own settings where possible, keep rules few and simple, and test changes in Google Search Console before relying on them.'],
  'taxi-private-hire-marketing-uk': ['Most taxi customers decide in seconds from the map results, so a complete Google Business Profile with the right number and steady reviews comes first.', 'Separate pages for airport transfers, business accounts, contract work and longer journeys attract higher-value bookings than a single homepage.', 'Any claims about licensing, safety or vehicles must be accurate and up to date, and firms should check current guidance from their licensing authority.'],
  'theatre-marketing-uk': ['Independent theatres sell most tickets to people who already know them, so a well-kept mailing list and an easy ticketing journey matter most.', 'Every show needs its own page with dates, prices, running time, age guidance and access information, written to answer the questions audiences ask.', 'Paid social and search ads work best when they target specific audiences for each production rather than promoting the whole season at once.'],
};
